{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - **Phase 2 of 2 — IMPLEMENTATION (TDD).** Implement 10 SOS cards: **1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257** in `/workspace/cards/sos/`. Each card directory has a `card_spec.json` (oracle text/details) and a `card_impl.py` template to fill in.\n   - Use completed FDN cards in `/workspace/cards/fdn/` as implementation examples; refer to `RULEBOOK.txt` for deep rules (via `grep-rulebook` skill).\n   - Follow `/workspace/PLAN.md` (read in full first). It has the engine-gap analysis, per-card plans (nearest FDN analogue + exact seams), and implementation order. If a point is wrong, correct course and note the deviation in PLAN.md.\n   - **Strict TDD**: vertical tracer-bullet, one failing test at a time through the engine's public interface (`test_utils`: create_game, set_board_state, cast_spell, advance_to_phase, declare_attackers, declare_blockers). Red → minimal green → repeat. Do NOT write all tests up front.\n   - Build shared engine seams FIRST, then cards simplest→hardest.\n   - **Discipline constraints (verbatim intent):** Test the real engine, not a stand-in — never hand-construct internal events, pop the stack and call on_resolve() directly, or script a player's internal queue. Reuse before you add; mirror nearest FDN card; keep engine edits minimal/additive. Requirements (card_spec.json + RULEBOOK.txt) are source of truth, not tests.\n   - **Guard the engine:** after each card and after any `engine/` change, run `python3 -m pytest engine_tests/ -q` — never ship a regression.\n   - **CRITICAL CONSTRAINT (security/integrity):** \"Do not modify any files under workspace/engine_tests/. These tests are staged for your local verification only; the runner uses its own authoritative copies for grading. Modifying the workspace tests will not change your score — it will only mislead you about whether your engine changes are correct.\" Also: never touch any `cards/fdn/fdn_*/tests.py`; never rename/move/delete existing `engine/` symbols (additive-only); keep each card class in `cards/sos/sos_<N>/card_impl.py`.\n   - Write `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py` per card covering golden path + edge cases.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - MTG engine: zones, stack (LIFO), triggered abilities (TriggerManager.fire_event), replacement effects (ReplacementManager.apply, \"instead\" semantics), continuous effects (7-layer system, EffectManager.apply_all reset-then-reapply), state-based actions.\n   - Casting pipeline: cast_spell (pays cost, sets colors_spent), cast_spell_free (no pay), _resolve_spell (sets chosen_targets, calls on_resolve, moves to bf/graveyard).\n   - Keyword enum (FLYING, FIRST_STRIKE, DOUBLE_STRIKE, DEATHTOUCH, TRAMPLE, LIFELINK, VIGILANCE, REACH, HASTE, FLASH, DEFENDER, HEXPROOF, INDESTRUCTIBLE, MENACE, WARD, PROWESS). Surveil/Converge/Affinity/Prepared/Paradigm/Miracle/Casualty are card-logic mechanics, NOT keyword flags.\n   - ManaCost.cmc = generic + sum(pips) + len(hybrid).\n   - colors_spent set by engine as `list(player.mana_pool.last_payment_colors)`; cleared by move_zone. Converge cards (fdn_205) read it as int when set by tests.\n   - TargetRequirement(filter_fn, description, zone); chosen targets read via self.chosen_targets in on_resolve.\n   - Triggered abilities have NO targeting step — effect(game) does its own choosing.\n   - LoyaltyAbility via LoyaltyAbilityInstance + activate_ability; reads pw._resolve_target/_resolve_targets.\n   - copy_spell(game, original, controller, new_targets) in stack.py returns a StackObject (must push yourself).\n   - DeterministicPlayer pops scripted answers from a deque for choose/choose_target/choose_yes_no/choose_card/assign_damage_order.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **/workspace/PLAN.md** — THE handoff. Section 1 engine gaps table (8 seams): (1) fire SpellCastTriggeredEvent in cast_spell AND cast_spell_free after stack.push; (2) fire AttacksTriggeredEvent in declare_attackers_step inside the `for attacker in chosen` loop; (3) add `player: Any = None` to BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent + pass game.active_player in turn.py; (4) NEW BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player=None, is_precombat=False) fired in run_turn for main phases before priority_loop; (5) external_cost_reduction hook on CardImpl (default 0) + aggregate in get_cost_reduction over controller's battlefield; (6) ManaPool.last_payment_total + set card.mana_spent in cast_spell; (7) GameState.skipped_turns dict + skip loop in advance_phase normal branch; (8) cast_with_alternative_cost(game, player, card, alt_cost) helper. Section 3 order: shared seams (1.external_cost_reduction, 2.mana_spent, 3.AttacksTriggeredEvent, 4.upkeep player, 5.main-phase event, 6.SpellCastTriggeredEvent, 7.cast_with_alternative_cost, 8.skipped_turns), then Group1 (sos_245, sos_4), Group2 (sos_226, sos_57, sos_1), Group3 (sos_257, sos_13), Group4 (sos_97, sos_201, sos_120).\n   - **engine/casting.py** — cast_spell (~line 246 push) and cast_spell_free (~line 371 push) need SpellCastTriggeredEvent fired. get_cost_reduction at line 89-108 (sets card.controller, calls card.cost_reduction, clamps to generic). Line 229 sets colors_spent. _PERMANENT_TYPES frozenset. _resolve_spell sets card.chosen_targets then on_resolve.\n   - **engine/events.py** — SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell, player, card, controller) and AttacksTriggeredEvent(creature, attacker) already exist. BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent currently `pass` (needs player field). MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent has mutable `destination` for redirection.\n   - **engine/triggers.py** — TriggerRegistration(event_type, condition, effect, source, controller). register/unregister(source identity)/fire_event (APNAP, isinstance subtype matching).\n   - **engine/combat.py** — declare_attackers_step lines 244-257: loop sets combat.attackers[attacker], is_attacking=True, taps unless VIGILANCE. AttacksTriggeredEvent must fire here.\n   - **engine/turn.py** — line 202-204 upkeep fires `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent()`. Line 207 combat dispatch. apply_all called line 136 in cleanup. Need main-phase event branch ~line 207.\n   - **engine/game_state.py** — __init__ has extra_turns=[], _normal_next_index=1. advance_phase normal branch lines 147-159 (else after extra_turns). Need skipped_turns dict + skip loop.\n   - **engine/mana.py** — ManaPool.pay (line 98) commits via working dict, computes _last_payment_colors. Need _last_payment_total tracking near line 162.\n   - **engine/stack.py** — copy_spell shallow-copies source, binds _copy_resolve (no zone move). priority_loop pops top and calls on_resolve.\n   - **engine/card.py** — CardImpl hooks: can_cast, cost_reduction (returns 0), on_cast, on_resolve, get_targets, register_triggers, register_replacement_effects, get_activated_abilities, get_modes. Creature has base_power/base_toughness/modified_power/modified_toughness/power(property)/toughness(property)/damage_marked/is_tapped/summoning_sick/is_attacking/is_blocking/plus_one_counters. _reset_characteristics resets card_types to _original_card_types and keywords (Creature also resets modified_power/toughness). Land.can_cast returns False; get_mana_abilities. Planeswalker has loyalty/starting_loyalty/get_loyalty_abilities.\n   - **engine/continuous_effects.py** — ContinuousEffect(source, layer, sublayer, apply, timestamp, duration). Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS=7, SubLayer.SET_PT=\"7b\", MODIFY_PT=\"7c\". DURATION_END_OF_TURN=0, DURATION_PERMANENT=-1. apply_all resets then applies in layer/sublayer/timestamp order.\n   - **engine/abilities.py** — activate_ability dispatches ActivatedAbilityInstance(cost(game,source)->bool, effect, is_mana_ability) or LoyaltyAbilityInstance(loyalty_cost, effect). Mana abilities resolve immediately; others push StackObject. Loyalty: sorcery-speed only, once-per-turn, loyalty can't go below 0.\n   - **engine/game.py** — draw_card increments player.cards_drawn_this_turn (created lazily) and fires DrawsCardTriggeredEvent. sacrifice/destroy/exile use move_to_zone with replacement events.\n   - **test_utils.py** — cast_spell finds card by name in hand, sets sorcery timing for non-instants, REQUIRES empty stack, scripts targets into player._script, then _resolve_top_of_stack (pops + on_resolve + SBAs). declare_attackers scripts active._script with attacker list. advance_to_phase fast-forwards.\n   - **engine_tests/test_extra_turns.py** — uses `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent()` no-arg construction implicitly via _make_game; extra_turns FIFO behavior MUST remain green (so player field must default None).\n   - **engine_tests/test_abilities.py** — shows LoyaltyAbilityInstance/ActivatedAbilityInstance/activate_ability usage patterns for tests.\n   - **FDN examples read:** fdn_48 Refute (`_counter_spell`, `_get_chosen_target`, can_cast/get_targets over game.stack.objects()); fdn_44 Kaito (get_loyalty_abilities, _resolve_target, SpellCastTriggeredEvent emblem); fdn_205 Wardens (colors_spent int, ETB tokens in on_resolve); fdn_167 Tolarian Terror (cost_reduction counts I/S in graveyard); fdn_6 Claws Out (cost_reduction affinity + EOT ContinuousEffect MODIFY_PT); fdn_141 Giada (get_mana_abilities ManaAbility cost(game,src)->bool); fdn_91 Kellan (get_activated_abilities ActivatedAbility cost(game)->bool, animate via subtype/P-T mutation); fdn_182 Reassembling Skeleton (get_activated_abilities cost(game,src)->bool pays mana, _effect moves graveyard→battlefield + register_triggers).\n   - **sos_257/card_spec.json** — oracle: \"{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color. Spend this mana only to cast an instant or sorcery spell.\\n{5}: If this land isn't a creature, it becomes a 2/4 Wizard creature with \\\"Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, this creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn.\\\" It's still a land.\" (animation is PERMANENT, no \"until end of turn\"; +1/+0 is EOT).\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors yet (still in reading/discovery phase; no tests or code written).\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Identified that SpellCastTriggeredEvent/AttacksTriggeredEvent exist but aren't fired — confirms PLAN's wiring tasks.\n   - Determined test_utils.cast_spell requires empty stack, so countering a spell-on-stack (sos_57) can't use test_utils.cast_spell for the countered spell already on stack — tests for counterspells will need a different setup approach.\n   - For sos_257 animation: analyzed that CardImpl._reset_characteristics resets card_types to {LAND} on every apply_all, so animation must be a permanent ContinuousEffect (layer TYPE re-adds CREATURE, layer 7b SET_PT sets power=2/toughness=4) to survive apply_all idempotently; +1/+0 uses 7c MODIFY_PT EOT effect; Land needs plain power/toughness/damage_marked attributes added. Plan to also set attrs directly in {5} effect so state is visible without apply_all.\n   - Confirmed colors_spent is preserved through on_resolve (move_to_zone clears it but runs AFTER on_resolve).\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - (System-reminder) Deferred tools available via ToolSearch; skills list (tdd, grep-rulebook, etc.).\n   - Main task message: \"# Phase 2 of 2 — IMPLEMENTATION (TDD)... Read /workspace/PLAN.md in full... strict TDD... Build the shared engine seams first... Test the real engine, not a stand-in... Reuse before you add... Requirements are the source of truth... Guard the engine... Do not modify anything under engine_tests/. The task follows. --- Implement the following SOS cards: 1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257 in /workspace/cards/sos/. Each card directory contains a card_spec.json with the card's details and a card_impl.py template to fill in. Use the completed FDN cards in /workspace/cards/fdn/ as implementation examples. Refer to RULEBOOK.txt... You are expected to make changes to the engine... Do not modify any files under workspace/engine_tests/. These tests are staged for your local verification only; the runner uses its own authoritative copies for grading. Modifying the workspace tests will not change your score — it will only mislead you about whether your engine changes are correct.\"\n   - (Final message) Instruction to produce this summary with TEXT ONLY, no tool calls.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Read remaining SOS card_spec.json files: sos_1, sos_4, sos_13, sos_57, sos_97, sos_120, sos_201, sos_226, sos_245 (and their card_impl.py templates).\n   - Read fdn_28 (surveil) example for sos_97 +1 / sos_201.\n   - Implement the 8 shared engine seams (additive only), running engine_tests after each.\n   - Implement all 10 SOS cards in PLAN order with TDD tests each.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Immediately before this summary, I was in the discovery phase reading FDN example cards. The last file read was `/workspace/cards/fdn/fdn_182/card_impl.py` (Reassembling Skeleton), which demonstrates the `get_activated_abilities` pattern with `cost(game, src) -> bool` that pays mana and `_effect` that moves a card from graveyard to battlefield (relevant to sos_97's −2 reanimation ability). No engine edits or card implementations have been started yet. I have read all core engine modules, test_utils, and most referenced FDN cards, but have NOT yet read the SOS card_spec.json files for cards other than sos_257, nor any sos card_impl.py templates, nor fdn_28 (surveil).\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Continue discovery by reading the remaining SOS card_spec.json files (sos_1, sos_4, sos_13, sos_57, sos_97, sos_120, sos_201, sos_226, sos_245) and a sos card_impl.py template to confirm template structure, plus fdn_28 for the surveil pattern. Then begin implementing the shared engine seams in PLAN Section 3 order, starting with seam #1 (external_cost_reduction hook on CardImpl + aggregation in get_cost_reduction) per: \"Group 0 — Shared engine seams (do first; unblocks everything)... 1. `external_cost_reduction` hook + `get_cost_reduction` aggregation (additive, low risk).\" After each seam, run `python3 -m pytest engine_tests/ -q` to confirm no regression, then proceed to Group 1 cards (sos_245 Witherbloom, sos_4 Together as One) with TDD. This is directly in line with the user's explicit request to \"Build the shared engine seams first, then the cards that reuse them\" following PLAN.md order.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /home/node/.claude/projects/-workspace/ccba73e9-54b6-4808-89ce-87e442914ff8.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ccba73e9-54b6-4808-89ce-87e442914ff8","uuid":"abe59b3e-59f2-461b-952c-02c74d3f27db","timestamp":"2026-06-04T07:28:18.924Z","isSynthetic":true}
