{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GmQUiMLTH84e5Bs5hN75YM","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# PLAN.md — SOS Card Implementation Plan\n2\t\n3\tImplementation handoff for 10 SOS cards: **1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257**.\n4\tThis file is the *entire* handoff — it is self-contained. Read `AGENTS.md` for the hard\n5\trules (additive-only engine edits; never touch `engine_tests/` or any `cards/fdn/fdn_*/tests.py`;\n6\tnever rename/move/delete existing `engine/` symbols; keep each card class in\n7\t`cards/sos/sos_<N>/card_impl.py`).\n8\t\n9\t## Conventions verified in the engine (read before coding)\n10\t\n11\t- `Keyword` enum (`engine/types.py:97`) only has FLYING, FIRST_STRIKE, DOUBLE_STRIKE,\n12\t  DEATHTOUCH, TRAMPLE, LIFELINK, VIGILANCE, REACH, HASTE, FLASH, DEFENDER, HEXPROOF,\n13\t  INDESTRUCTIBLE, MENACE, WARD, PROWESS. **Surveil, Converge, Affinity, Prepared,\n14\t  Paradigm, Miracle, Casualty are NOT keyword flags** — they are mechanics handled by\n15\t  card logic. The `keywords` arrays in `card_spec.json` are Scryfall data; only map the\n16\t  real flags (Flying/Haste/Vigilance/Deathtouch/Reach) into `Keyword`.\n17\t- `ManaCost.cmc` property exists (`= generic + sum(pips) + len(hybrid)`), use it for MV.\n18\t- Casting pipeline (`engine/casting.py`): `cast_spell` already sets\n19\t  `card.colors_spent = list(player.mana_pool.last_payment_colors)` (a list of `Color`)\n20\t  after payment. `cast_spell_free(game, player, card, from_zone)` casts without paying.\n21\t  `_resolve_spell` sets `card.chosen_targets = stack_obj.targets` just before\n22\t  `card.on_resolve(game)`.\n23\t- Targets: `get_targets(game)` returns a list of\n24\t  `TargetRequirement(filter_fn, description, zone)` (`engine/types.py:239`). The chosen\n25\t  objects are read in `on_resolve` via `self.chosen_targets` (see `_get_chosen_target`\n26\t  helper in `cards/fdn/fdn_48/card_impl.py`).\n27\t- Triggered abilities have **no targeting step** — a trigger's `effect(game)` does any\n28\t  choosing itself (e.g. `controller.choose_card(...)`, `controller.choose_yes_no(...)`).\n29\t- Loyalty abilities: `get_loyalty_abilities()` returns `LoyaltyAbility(loyalty_cost,\n30\t  effect, description)`. Activation goes through `engine/abilities.py:activate_ability`\n31\t  with a `LoyaltyAbilityInstance`. Effects read targets from attributes set on the pw\n32\t  (`pw._resolve_target`), exactly like `cards/fdn/fdn_44/card_impl.py`.\n33\t- Helper actions in `engine/game.py`: `draw_card, discard, create_token, deal_damage,\n34\t  destroy, sacrifice, exile, add_counter, remove_counter, tap, untap`. `move_to_zone`\n35\t  (`engine/zones.py`) is the central transition and honors replacement effects.\n36\t- `copy_spell(game, original, controller, new_targets)` lives in `engine/stack.py`\n37\t  (used for casualty copies).\n38\t\n39\t---\n40\t\n41\t## Section 1 — Engine gaps\n42\t\n43\t| Capability needed | Smallest change | Engine file / seam | Cards that reuse it |\n44\t|---|---|---|---|\n45\t| Spell-cast triggers must actually fire | After `game.stack.push(stack_obj)` in **both** `cast_spell` and `cast_spell_free`, call `game.trigger_manager.fire_event(game, SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell=stack_obj, player=player, card=card, controller=player))`. | `engine/casting.py` (end of `cast_spell` ~line 246; end of `cast_spell_free` ~line 371) | sos_226 (casualty), sos_257 (animated +1/+0), sos_97 emblem-style not used; also un-breaks fdn_44/fdn_122 |\n46\t| Attacks triggers must fire | In `declare_attackers_step`, for each registered attacker fire `AttacksTriggeredEvent(creature=attacker, attacker=attacker)` (after setting `is_attacking`/tapping, inside the `for attacker in chosen` loop). | `engine/combat.py:244-257` | sos_1 |\n47\t| Upkeep trigger needs to know whose upkeep | Add field `player: Any = None` to `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent`; in turn.py fire `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent(player=game.active_player)`. Default keeps `test_extra_turns.py`'s no-arg construction valid. | `engine/events.py:70`, `engine/turn.py:204` | sos_201 |\n48\t| Beginning-of-main-phase delayed triggers | Add new event `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player=None, is_precombat=False)` in events.py; in `run_turn`, when `game.phase in (PRECOMBAT_MAIN, POSTCOMBAT_MAIN) and game.step is None`, fire it with `player=game.active_player, is_precombat=(phase==PRECOMBAT_MAIN)` *before* `priority_loop`. | `engine/events.py`, `engine/turn.py` (new branch in the dispatch ~line 207) | sos_57 (next main phase mana), sos_120 (Paradigm each first main phase) |\n49\t| Cost reduction granted by *other* permanents | Extend `get_cost_reduction`: after `raw = card.cost_reduction(game)`, also iterate `controller`'s battlefield and sum `obj.external_cost_reduction(game, card, controller)` for any obj exposing it. Add a default `external_cost_reduction(self, game, card, controller) -> int: return 0` on `CardImpl`. Clamp total to generic as today. | `engine/casting.py:89-108`, `engine/card.py` (new no-op hook) | sos_245 (grants affinity to your I/S spells) |\n50\t| \"Amount of mana spent\" to cast a spell | In `ManaPool.pay`, also record `self._last_payment_total = sum(old_pool.values()) - sum(working.values())`; expose `last_payment_total` property. In `cast_spell`, after payment set `card.mana_spent = player.mana_pool.last_payment_total`. (Free casts: leave `mana_spent` unset/0.) | `engine/mana.py` (in `pay`, near `_last_payment_colors`), `engine/casting.py:229` | sos_57 |\n51\t| Skip a player's next N turns | Add `self.skipped_turns: dict[int, int] = {}` in `GameState.__init__`. In `advance_phase`'s **normal** branch (the `else` after `extra_turns`), loop: take candidate `= self._normal_next_index`, toggle `_normal_next_index`; if `skipped_turns.get(candidate,0) > 0`, decrement it and `continue` (that player's turn is skipped, the other player becomes active next iteration); else set `active_player_index = candidate` and break. Do not touch the `extra_turns` branch. | `engine/game_state.py:75-83, 147-159` | sos_97 (−7) |\n52\t| Cast for an alternative cost (miracle) | Add helper `cast_with_alternative_cost(game, player, card, alt_cost)` mirroring `cast_spell` but paying `alt_cost` instead of `card.mana_cost` (reuse the same target/protection/push flow). | `engine/casting.py` (new function) | sos_201 (miracle {2}) |\n53\t\n54\tNotes:\n55\t- All new events fire harmlessly when no trigger is registered (verified `fire_event`\n56\t  early-returns on no match). Firing `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` is the only addition that\n57\t  could surface a latent trigger — confirm `pytest engine_tests` stays green right after\n58\t  wiring each seam.\n59\t- `cast_spell_free` already exists; sos_1 / sos_120 reuse it directly.\n60\t- The exile-instead-of-graveyard redirect (sos_1) reuses the existing\n61\t  `MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent` (`destination` mutated to `\"exile\"`).\n62\t\n63\t---\n64\t\n65\t## Section 2 — Per-card plan\n66\t\n67\t### sos_226 — Silverquill, the Disputant `{2}{W}{B}` 4/4 Elder Dragon (medium)\n68\t- **Clauses:** Flying, vigilance. \"Each instant and sorcery spell you cast has casualty 1\n69\t  (sacrifice a creature with power ≥1 → copy the spell, may choose new targets).\"\n70\t- **FDN analogue:** trigger registration like `cards/fdn/fdn_44` (SpellCastTriggeredEvent\n71\t  consumer); copy via `engine/stack.copy_spell` like casualty references.\n72\t- **Seams:** `Creature` with `keywords=Keyword.FLYING|Keyword.VIGILANCE`.\n73\t  `register_triggers`: register a `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` trigger (source=self,\n74\t  controller=self.controller). **Requires gap \"spell-cast triggers fire\".** Condition:\n75\t  `event.controller is self.controller` and `event.card.card_types & {INSTANT, SORCERY}`\n76\t  and `event.spell is not self`-cast-irrelevant. Effect: find a creature you control with\n77\t  `power >= 1`; `controller.choose_yes_no(\"Casualty 1: sacrifice a creature to copy?\")`;\n78\t  if yes, pick the creature (`choose_card`), `sacrifice(game, controller, creature)`,\n79\t  then `game.stack.push(copy_spell(game, event.spell, controller,\n80\t  new_targets=event.spell.targets))`.\n81\t- **Edge cases:** `copy_spell` *returns* a `StackObject` but does NOT push it — you must\n82\t  `game.stack.push(...)` the result yourself. Pushing it puts the copy on top of the\n83\t  original so it resolves first. No eligible creature → no offer; the dragon itself can be\n84\t  the sacrifice. Don't offer casualty for the dragon's own spell (it's a creature, not I/S).\n85\t\n86\t### sos_245 — Witherbloom, the Balancer `{6}{B}{G}` 5/5 Elder Dragon (complex)\n87\t- **Clauses:** Affinity for creatures (self, {1} less per creature you control). Flying,\n88\t  deathtouch. \"Instant and sorcery spells you cast have affinity for creatures.\"\n89\t- **FDN analogue:** `cards/fdn/fdn_6` (ClawsOut) for affinity-as-`cost_reduction`.\n90\t- **Seams:** `keywords=Keyword.FLYING|Keyword.DEATHTOUCH`.\n91\t  Own affinity: override `cost_reduction(game)` = count creatures `self.controller`\n92\t  controls (battlefield, `CardType.CREATURE in card_types`). Granting affinity to your\n93\t  I/S spells: implement `external_cost_reduction(self, game, card, controller)` returning\n94\t  the creature count when `controller is self.controller` and\n95\t  `card.card_types & {INSTANT, SORCERY}`, else 0. **Requires gap \"external cost\n96\t  reduction\".**\n97\t- **Edge cases:** while Witherbloom is on the stack (being cast), it's not yet a creature\n98\t  you control — its own affinity counts other creatures only (battlefield query naturally\n99\t  excludes the stack). Clamp handled by `get_cost_reduction`. Don't double-count if both\n100\t  self `cost_reduction` and external apply (they apply to different cards).\n101\t\n102\t### sos_4 — Together as One `{6}` Sorcery (complex)\n103\t- **Clauses:** Converge — target player draws X, deals X damage to any target, you gain X\n104\t  life; X = number of colors of mana spent to cast this spell.\n105\t- **FDN analogue:** `cards/fdn/fdn_205` (colors_spent). Targeting like `fdn_48`.\n106\t- **Seams:** `Sorcery`. `get_targets`: two `TargetRequirement`s — (1) a player (zone\n107\t  BATTLEFIELD or however players are targeted; use a player filter), (2) \"any target\"\n108\t  (creature OR player; filter accepts objects with `damage_marked` or `life`).\n109\t  `on_resolve`: compute `cs = self.colors_spent`; `X = len(cs) if isinstance(cs, list)\n110\t  else int(cs or 0)` (engine sets a list; FDN test convention uses int — handle both).\n111\t  Then `draw_card` X times for chosen player; `deal_damage(game, self, any_target, X)`;\n112\t  `self.controller.life += X`.\n113\t- **Edge cases:** X=0 when only generic/no colored mana spent → all three sub-effects are\n114\t  no-ops (loops run 0 times, deal_damage(≤0) returns early). Order: draw, then damage,\n115\t  then life (as printed). Damage target may be the same player who draws.\n116\t\n117\t### sos_57 — Mana Sculpt `{1}{U}{U}` Instant (medium)\n118\t- **Clauses:** Counter target spell. If you control a Wizard, add {C} equal to the amount\n119\t  of mana spent to cast that spell at the beginning of your next main phase.\n120\t- **FDN analogue:** `cards/fdn/fdn_48` (Refute) for counter-target-spell\n121\t  (`can_cast`/`get_targets` over `game.stack.objects()`, `_counter_spell` helper).\n122\t- **Seams:** `Instant`. Copy the `_counter_spell` / `_get_chosen_target` helpers pattern\n123\t  from fdn_48. In `on_resolve`: capture `countered = target.source` and\n124\t  `spent = getattr(countered, \"mana_spent\", 0)` **before** countering (needs gap\n125\t  \"amount of mana spent\"). Counter the spell. If `self.controller` controls a Wizard\n126\t  (`\"Wizard\" in obj.subtypes` on battlefield), register a one-shot\n127\t  `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` trigger (needs gap \"beginning-of-main-phase\n128\t  event\") whose condition is `event.player is self.controller`; effect adds\n129\t  `ManaType.COLORLESS` × `spent` to the controller's pool and then unregisters itself\n130\t  (`game.trigger_manager.unregister(marker_source)`).\n131\t- **Edge cases:** no Wizard → no delayed mana. \"next main phase\" = first main phase of\n132\t  either player where the controller is active; one-shot (unregister after firing). If the\n133\t  countered spell was itself free-cast, `mana_spent` is 0 → adds nothing.\n134\t\n135\t### sos_1 — The Dawning Archaic `{10}` 7/7 Legendary Avatar (complex)\n136\t- **Clauses:** Costs {1} less per instant/sorcery card in your graveyard. Reach. \"Whenever\n137\t  this attacks, you may cast target I/S from your graveyard without paying its mana cost.\n138\t  If that spell would be put into your graveyard, exile it instead.\"\n139\t- **FDN analogue:** `cards/fdn/fdn_167` (Tolarian Terror) for the graveyard-count\n140\t  `cost_reduction`. `cast_spell_free` for the free cast.\n141\t- **Seams:** `Creature(keywords=Keyword.REACH, base_power=7, base_toughness=7,\n142\t  supertypes={Supertype.LEGENDARY})`. `cost_reduction(game)`: count I/S in\n143\t  `self.controller` graveyard (copy fdn_167). `register_triggers`: register an\n144\t  `AttacksTriggeredEvent` trigger (needs gap \"attacks triggers fire\"); condition\n145\t  `event.creature is self`. Effect: gather I/S cards in controller's graveyard; if any and\n146\t  `choose_yes_no`, pick one (`choose_card`), register a card-specific\n147\t  `MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent` replacement that redirects *that card* to exile\n148\t  (set `destination=\"exile\"`), then `cast_spell_free(game, controller, chosen,\n149\t  Zone.GRAVEYARD)`.\n150\t- **Edge cases:** empty graveyard → no trigger effect. The exile-redirect replacement must\n151\t  match only the chosen card (filter by identity) and be self-unregistering after it fires\n152\t  once. Reach is purely a blocking keyword (already handled in `combat._can_block`). The\n153\t  cost reduction only reduces generic (the whole cost is generic {10}).\n154\t\n155\t### sos_13 — Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares `{1}{W}{W} // {W}` (complex)\n156\t- **Clauses:** Front: Creature — Cat Cleric, 3/3 white. ETB: target player creates a 1/1\n157\t  W/B Inkling token with flying; then if an opponent controls more creatures than you,\n158\t  this creature becomes *prepared*. While prepared, you may cast a copy of its spell\n159\t  (Swords to Plowshares: exile target creature, its controller gains life = its power);\n160\t  casting the copy unprepares it.\n161\t- **FDN analogue:** ETB token creation like `create_token`; activated-ability gating like\n162\t  `cards/fdn/fdn_91` (Kellan) state-flag pattern; targeting like fdn_48.\n163\t- **Seams:** `Creature` front class (the canonical class in this file). Set `self.is_prepared\n164\t  = False` in `__init__`. `register_triggers`: ETB trigger (`EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent`,\n165\t  condition `event.permanent is self`). Effect: choose target player, `create_token` a 1/1\n166\t  flier (`Creature(name=\"Inkling\", base_power=1, base_toughness=1, keywords=Keyword.FLYING)`,\n167\t  colors W/B noted in rules_text); then count creatures: if `opp_creatures > my_creatures`,\n168\t  `self.is_prepared = True`. `get_activated_abilities`: one ability available only when\n169\t  `self.is_prepared` (cost returns False otherwise) — sorcery-speed copy-of-spell:\n170\t  put a Swords effect on the stack (choose target creature; `exile(game, creature)`; that\n171\t  creature's controller `.life += power`), then set `self.is_prepared = False`.\n172\t- **Edge cases:** \"more creatures than you\" strictly greater; the token counts toward\n173\t  *your* count only after it's created (it enters under the *target player*'s control —\n174\t  if you targeted yourself it raises your count). Casting the copy when not prepared is\n175\t  illegal (cost guard). Keep entire DFC behavior card-local; only ETB + targeting + token\n176\t  + exile engine helpers are reused.\n177\t\n178\t### sos_120 — Improvisation Capstone `{5}{R}{R}` Sorcery — Lesson (complex)\n179\t- **Clauses:** Exile from top of library until total MV ≥ 4; you may cast any number of\n180\t  them for free. Paradigm: exile this spell; after you first resolve a spell with this\n181\t  name, you may cast a copy of it from exile for free at the beginning of each of your\n182\t  first main phases.\n183\t- **FDN analogue:** `cast_spell_free` for the free casts; main-phase delayed trigger\n184\t  (new event); MV via `ManaCost.cmc`.\n185\t- **Seams:** `Sorcery`. `on_resolve`: from `self.controller` library top, move cards to\n186\t  exile (`move_to_zone(... Zone.LIBRARY, Zone.EXILE)`) accumulating `cmc` until total ≥ 4;\n187\t  for each exiled card that is castable, offer `choose_yes_no` then\n188\t  `cast_spell_free(game, controller, c, Zone.EXILE)`. Paradigm: after resolving, exile\n189\t  *this* card (the engine would send a sorcery to graveyard — override by moving self to\n190\t  exile in `on_resolve`/via replacement) and register a repeating\n191\t  `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` trigger (needs gap \"main-phase event\"), condition\n192\t  `event.player is controller and event.is_precombat`, effect: offer to cast a copy of\n193\t  this card from exile for free.\n194\t- **Edge cases:** library runs out before reaching MV 4 → stop. Lands among exiled cards\n195\t  can't be \"cast\" (skip — only cast spells). Paradigm copy is a *copy* (don't move the\n196\t  exiled original; create a token-copy or re-castable copy). \"First resolve\" → register the\n197\t  Paradigm trigger only once. This is the hardest part; Paradigm may be implemented after\n198\t  the base spell works.\n199\t\n200\t### sos_201 — Lorehold, the Historian `{3}{R}{W}` 5/5 Elder Dragon (expert)\n201\t- **Clauses:** Flying, haste. \"Each instant and sorcery card in your hand has miracle {2}.\"\n202\t  \"At the beginning of each opponent's upkeep, you may discard a card; if you do, draw a\n203\t  card.\"\n204\t- **FDN analogue:** opponent-upkeep loot — `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent`/upkeep trigger\n205\t  patterns (fdn_28 surveil shows draw-trigger + choose plumbing); miracle uses the new\n206\t  `cast_with_alternative_cost`.\n207\t- **Seams:** `keywords=Keyword.FLYING|Keyword.HASTE`. `register_triggers`: (a)\n208\t  `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent` trigger (needs gap \"upkeep player field\"); condition\n209\t  `event.player is not self.controller`; effect: `choose_yes_no` → if yes pick a card to\n210\t  discard (`choose_card`), `discard`, then `draw_card`. (b) Miracle: register a\n211\t  `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent` trigger; condition: `event.player is self.controller`, the\n212\t  drawn `event.card` is I/S and owned by controller, and it is the first card drawn this\n213\t  turn (`event.player.cards_drawn_this_turn == 1` — engine increments before firing).\n214\t  Effect: `choose_yes_no(\"Cast for miracle {2}?\")`; if yes,\n215\t  `cast_with_alternative_cost(game, controller, event.card, ManaCost(generic=2))`.\n216\t- **Edge cases:** miracle only applies while Lorehold is on the battlefield and the card is\n217\t  in *your* hand at draw time. Only the first draw of the turn qualifies. Opponent-upkeep\n218\t  loot is \"may\" and only draws if you discarded. Haste lets the dragon attack the turn it\n219\t  enters (engine already keys off `summoning_sick`+HASTE). Miracle is the hardest sub-part\n220\t  — land the upkeep loot + keywords first.\n221\t\n222\t### sos_97 — Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer `{1}{B}{B}` Planeswalker, loyalty 3 (expert)\n223\t- **Clauses:** +1 Surveil 2. −1 any number of target players each discard a card. −2\n224\t  return target creature card MV ≤ 3 from your graveyard to the battlefield. −7 flip five\n225\t  coins; target opponent skips their next X turns (X = heads).\n226\t- **FDN analogue:** `cards/fdn/fdn_44` (Kaito) for `get_loyalty_abilities` + `_resolve_target`\n227\t  pattern; `cards/fdn/fdn_28` for surveil; `cards/fdn/fdn_182` for graveyard→battlefield\n228\t  return.\n229\t- **Seams:** `Planeswalker(starting_loyalty=3, supertypes={Supertype.LEGENDARY},\n230\t  subtypes={\"Ral\"})`. `get_loyalty_abilities` returns four `LoyaltyAbility`:\n231\t  - `+1` Surveil 2: look at top 2 of controller's library, for each `choose_yes_no` to put\n232\t    in graveyard (fdn_28 pattern extended to 2 cards).\n233\t  - `−1`: for each target player (read from `pw._resolve_targets` list; default both / the\n234\t    chosen subset), that player `choose_card`+`discard` one card.\n235\t  - `−2`: read `pw._resolve_target` (a creature card in controller's graveyard with\n236\t    `mana_cost.cmc <= 3`); remove from graveyard and put onto battlefield under\n237\t    controller (`move_to_zone(... GRAVEYARD, BATTLEFIELD)` or graveyard.remove + bf.add +\n238\t    register triggers, like fdn_182).\n239\t  - `−7`: flip 5 coins (`random`), `heads = sum`; choose target opponent; set\n240\t    `game.skipped_turns[opp_index] = game.skipped_turns.get(opp_index,0) + heads`\n241\t    (needs gap \"skip turns\").\n242\t- **Activation/tests:** loyalty abilities are activated by constructing\n243\t  `LoyaltyAbilityInstance(source=pw, controller=ctrl, loyalty_cost=ab.loyalty_cost,\n244\t  effect=ab.effect)` and calling `engine/abilities.activate_ability`; set `pw._resolve_target`\n245\t  / `pw._resolve_targets` before activation (fdn_44 convention).\n246\t- **Edge cases:** −2 filter must reject MV > 3 and non-creatures. −7 X can be 0 (no heads)\n247\t  → no skip. Skip mechanic in a 2-player game means the opponent's queued turns are\n248\t  consumed and the active player effectively takes consecutive turns; verify against the\n249\t  `advance_phase` normal-branch loop. Loyalty cost can't drop below 0 (engine enforces).\n250\t\n251\t### sos_257 — Great Hall of the Biblioplex — Land (complex)\n252\t- **Clauses:** `{T}: Add {C}`. `{T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color; spend only on\n253\t  an I/S spell.` `{5}: If not already a creature, becomes a 2/4 Wizard creature with\n254\t  \"Whenever you cast an I/S spell, this gets +1/+0 until end of turn\"; still a land.`\n255\t- **FDN analogue:** `cards/fdn/fdn_141` (Giada) for `get_mana_abilities` (tap cost +\n256\t  restricted-mana note); `cards/fdn/fdn_91` (Kellan) for the animate-via-activated-ability\n257\t  mutation pattern; `cards/fdn/fdn_6` end-of-turn `ContinuousEffect` for the +1/+0.\n258\t- **Seams:** `Land`. `get_mana_abilities`: (1) `{T}: Add {C}` — `cost` taps, `mana_produced`\n259\t  adds `ManaType.COLORLESS`. (2) `{T}, Pay 1 life` — `cost` taps + `controller.life -= 1`;\n260\t  `mana_produced` adds a chosen color. (The \"spend only on I/S\" restriction is a known\n261\t  engine simplification — note it in rules_text; the mana pool has no restriction tags, so\n262\t  model best-effort or document the gap.) `get_activated_abilities`: `{5}` ability — `cost`\n263\t  pays `ManaCost(generic=5)` from pool; `effect`: if `CardType.CREATURE not in\n264\t  self.card_types`, add CREATURE to `card_types`, set `subtypes |= {\"Wizard\"}`,\n265\t  set `base_power`/`base_toughness`-style fields (note: `Land` is not a `Creature`, so the\n266\t  implementer must attach `modified_power=2`/`modified_toughness=4` and the combat-required\n267\t  attrs, or model the animated state carefully — simplest: give the Land the creature\n268\t  attributes it needs: `base_power=2, base_toughness=4, modified_power=2,\n269\t  modified_toughness=4, damage_marked=0, summoning_sick=...`, since combat eligibility keys\n270\t  off `hasattr(c, \"base_power\")`). Register a `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` trigger (needs gap\n271\t  \"spell-cast triggers fire\") that, while animated and `event.controller is self.controller`\n272\t  and `event.card` is I/S, adds an end-of-turn `ContinuousEffect` (Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS /\n273\t  SubLayer.MODIFY_PT) granting +1/+0.\n274\t- **Edge cases:** `{5}` is idempotent if already a creature (guard on CREATURE in\n275\t  card_types). The +1/+0 must be until end of turn (use `DURATION_END_OF_TURN`). Animating\n276\t  doesn't remove LAND, and lands have summoning sickness for *attacking* but tapping for\n277\t  mana is unaffected (the {T} mana abilities still work while animated). The\n278\t  spell-cast +1/+0 trigger should only do anything while the land is currently a creature.\n279\t\n280\t---\n281\t\n282\t## Section 3 — Implementation order\n283\t\n284\tDo shared engine work first, then cards simplest→hardest. After each engine seam, run\n285\t`pytest engine_tests` to confirm nothing regressed (especially after wiring\n286\t`SpellCastTriggeredEvent`).\n287\t\n288\t**Group 0 — Shared engine seams (do first; unblocks everything).**\n289\tRationale: every card below depends on at least one. Implement and regression-test in this\n290\torder so failures are isolated:\n291\t1. `external_cost_reduction` hook + `get_cost_reduction` aggregation (additive, low risk).\n292\t2. `mana_spent` tracking (`ManaPool.last_payment_total` + set in `cast_spell`).\n293\t3. `AttacksTriggeredEvent` firing in `declare_attackers_step`.\n294\t4. `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent.player` field + pass active player.\n295\t5. `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` new event + fire in `run_turn`.\n296\t6. `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` firing in `cast_spell`/`cast_spell_free` (highest blast\n297\t   radius — test immediately).\n298\t7. `cast_with_alternative_cost` helper.\n299\t8. `skipped_turns` + `advance_phase` skip loop.\n300\t\n301\t**Group 1 — Pure keyword / cost-reduction cards (simplest).**\n302\tRationale: validate the engine seams with the least extra logic.\n303\t- **sos_245 Witherbloom** (affinity self + external; Flying/Deathtouch keywords).\n304\t- **sos_4 Together as One** (Converge via existing `colors_spent`; just targeting + math).\n305\t\n306\t**Group 2 — Single-mechanic cards.**\n307\t- **sos_226 Silverquill** (casualty via spell-cast trigger + `copy_spell`).\n308\t- **sos_57 Mana Sculpt** (counterspell via fdn_48 + delayed main-phase mana).\n309\t- **sos_1 The Dawning Archaic** (graveyard cost-reduction + attacks trigger free-cast +\n310\t  exile replacement).\n311\t\n312\t**Group 3 — Multi-clause permanents.**\n313\t- **sos_257 Great Hall** (mana abilities + animate + spell-cast +1/+0 trigger).\n314\t- **sos_13 Emeritus of Truce** (ETB token + prepared activated copy-spell).\n315\t\n316\t**Group 4 — Expert / multi-system (hardest, last).**\n317\tRationale: each combines several seams and has the most edge cases.\n318\t- **sos_97 Ral Zarek** (4 loyalty abilities incl. surveil, reanimation w/ MV filter, and\n319\t  the skip-turns ultimate).\n320\t- **sos_201 Lorehold** (opponent-upkeep loot via upkeep-player field + miracle via\n321\t  `cast_with_alternative_cost` on the draw trigger).\n322\t- **sos_120 Improvisation Capstone** (exile-until-MV free casts + Paradigm repeating\n323\t  main-phase copy) — most novel control flow; finish last.\n324\t\n325\tFor each card: write `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py` covering the golden path + the listed\n326\tedge cases, and run `pytest cards/sos/sos_<N>` plus the full `pytest` before moving on.\n327\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ccba73e9-54b6-4808-89ce-87e442914ff8","uuid":"072a4f5b-db94-44f9-9087-e4ff46f9c8b5","timestamp":"2026-06-04T07:28:34.050Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/PLAN.md","content":"# PLAN.md — SOS Card Implementation Plan\n\nImplementation handoff for 10 SOS cards: **1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257**.\nThis file is the *entire* handoff — it is self-contained. Read `AGENTS.md` for the hard\nrules (additive-only engine edits; never touch `engine_tests/` or any `cards/fdn/fdn_*/tests.py`;\nnever rename/move/delete existing `engine/` symbols; keep each card class in\n`cards/sos/sos_<N>/card_impl.py`).\n\n## Conventions verified in the engine (read before coding)\n\n- `Keyword` enum (`engine/types.py:97`) only has FLYING, FIRST_STRIKE, DOUBLE_STRIKE,\n  DEATHTOUCH, TRAMPLE, LIFELINK, VIGILANCE, REACH, HASTE, FLASH, DEFENDER, HEXPROOF,\n  INDESTRUCTIBLE, MENACE, WARD, PROWESS. **Surveil, Converge, Affinity, Prepared,\n  Paradigm, Miracle, Casualty are NOT keyword flags** — they are mechanics handled by\n  card logic. The `keywords` arrays in `card_spec.json` are Scryfall data; only map the\n  real flags (Flying/Haste/Vigilance/Deathtouch/Reach) into `Keyword`.\n- `ManaCost.cmc` property exists (`= generic + sum(pips) + len(hybrid)`), use it for MV.\n- Casting pipeline (`engine/casting.py`): `cast_spell` already sets\n  `card.colors_spent = list(player.mana_pool.last_payment_colors)` (a list of `Color`)\n  after payment. `cast_spell_free(game, player, card, from_zone)` casts without paying.\n  `_resolve_spell` sets `card.chosen_targets = stack_obj.targets` just before\n  `card.on_resolve(game)`.\n- Targets: `get_targets(game)` returns a list of\n  `TargetRequirement(filter_fn, description, zone)` (`engine/types.py:239`). The chosen\n  objects are read in `on_resolve` via `self.chosen_targets` (see `_get_chosen_target`\n  helper in `cards/fdn/fdn_48/card_impl.py`).\n- Triggered abilities have **no targeting step** — a trigger's `effect(game)` does any\n  choosing itself (e.g. `controller.choose_card(...)`, `controller.choose_yes_no(...)`).\n- Loyalty abilities: `get_loyalty_abilities()` returns `LoyaltyAbility(loyalty_cost,\n  effect, description)`. Activation goes through `engine/abilities.py:activate_ability`\n  with a `LoyaltyAbilityInstance`. Effects read targets from attributes set on the pw\n  (`pw._resolve_target`), exactly like `cards/fdn/fdn_44/card_impl.py`.\n- Helper actions in `engine/game.py`: `draw_card, discard, create_token, deal_damage,\n  destroy, sacrifice, exile, add_counter, remove_counter, tap, untap`. `move_to_zone`\n  (`engine/zones.py`) is the central transition and honors replacement effects.\n- `copy_spell(game, original, controller, new_targets)` lives in `engine/stack.py`\n  (used for casualty copies).\n\n---\n\n## Section 1 — Engine gaps\n\n| Capability needed | Smallest change | Engine file / seam | Cards that reuse it |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Spell-cast triggers must actually fire | After `game.stack.push(stack_obj)` in **both** `cast_spell` and `cast_spell_free`, call `game.trigger_manager.fire_event(game, SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell=stack_obj, player=player, card=card, controller=player))`. | `engine/casting.py` (end of `cast_spell` ~line 246; end of `cast_spell_free` ~line 371) | sos_226 (casualty), sos_257 (animated +1/+0), sos_97 emblem-style not used; also un-breaks fdn_44/fdn_122 |\n| Attacks triggers must fire | In `declare_attackers_step`, for each registered attacker fire `AttacksTriggeredEvent(creature=attacker, attacker=attacker)` (after setting `is_attacking`/tapping, inside the `for attacker in chosen` loop). | `engine/combat.py:244-257` | sos_1 |\n| Upkeep trigger needs to know whose upkeep | Add field `player: Any = None` to `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent`; in turn.py fire `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent(player=game.active_player)`. Default keeps `test_extra_turns.py`'s no-arg construction valid. | `engine/events.py:70`, `engine/turn.py:204` | sos_201 |\n| Beginning-of-main-phase delayed triggers | Add new event `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player=None, is_precombat=False)` in events.py; in `run_turn`, when `game.phase in (PRECOMBAT_MAIN, POSTCOMBAT_MAIN) and game.step is None`, fire it with `player=game.active_player, is_precombat=(phase==PRECOMBAT_MAIN)` *before* `priority_loop`. | `engine/events.py`, `engine/turn.py` (new branch in the dispatch ~line 207) | sos_57 (next main phase mana), sos_120 (Paradigm each first main phase) |\n| Cost reduction granted by *other* permanents | Extend `get_cost_reduction`: after `raw = card.cost_reduction(game)`, also iterate `controller`'s battlefield and sum `obj.external_cost_reduction(game, card, controller)` for any obj exposing it. Add a default `external_cost_reduction(self, game, card, controller) -> int: return 0` on `CardImpl`. Clamp total to generic as today. | `engine/casting.py:89-108`, `engine/card.py` (new no-op hook) | sos_245 (grants affinity to your I/S spells) |\n| \"Amount of mana spent\" to cast a spell | In `ManaPool.pay`, also record `self._last_payment_total = sum(old_pool.values()) - sum(working.values())`; expose `last_payment_total` property. In `cast_spell`, after payment set `card.mana_spent = player.mana_pool.last_payment_total`. (Free casts: leave `mana_spent` unset/0.) | `engine/mana.py` (in `pay`, near `_last_payment_colors`), `engine/casting.py:229` | sos_57 |\n| Skip a player's next N turns | Add `self.skipped_turns: dict[int, int] = {}` in `GameState.__init__`. In `advance_phase`'s **normal** branch (the `else` after `extra_turns`), loop: take candidate `= self._normal_next_index`, toggle `_normal_next_index`; if `skipped_turns.get(candidate,0) > 0`, decrement it and `continue` (that player's turn is skipped, the other player becomes active next iteration); else set `active_player_index = candidate` and break. Do not touch the `extra_turns` branch. | `engine/game_state.py:75-83, 147-159` | sos_97 (−7) |\n| Cast for an alternative cost (miracle) | Add helper `cast_with_alternative_cost(game, player, card, alt_cost)` mirroring `cast_spell` but paying `alt_cost` instead of `card.mana_cost` (reuse the same target/protection/push flow). | `engine/casting.py` (new function) | sos_201 (miracle {2}) |\n\nNotes:\n- All new events fire harmlessly when no trigger is registered (verified `fire_event`\n  early-returns on no match). Firing `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` is the only addition that\n  could surface a latent trigger — confirm `pytest engine_tests` stays green right after\n  wiring each seam.\n- `cast_spell_free` already exists; sos_1 / sos_120 reuse it directly.\n- The exile-instead-of-graveyard redirect (sos_1) reuses the existing\n  `MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent` (`destination` mutated to `\"exile\"`).\n\n---\n\n## Section 2 — Per-card plan\n\n### sos_226 — Silverquill, the Disputant `{2}{W}{B}` 4/4 Elder Dragon (medium)\n- **Clauses:** Flying, vigilance. \"Each instant and sorcery spell you cast has casualty 1\n  (sacrifice a creature with power ≥1 → copy the spell, may choose new targets).\"\n- **FDN analogue:** trigger registration like `cards/fdn/fdn_44` (SpellCastTriggeredEvent\n  consumer); copy via `engine/stack.copy_spell` like casualty references.\n- **Seams:** `Creature` with `keywords=Keyword.FLYING|Keyword.VIGILANCE`.\n  `register_triggers`: register a `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` trigger (source=self,\n  controller=self.controller). **Requires gap \"spell-cast triggers fire\".** Condition:\n  `event.controller is self.controller` and `event.card.card_types & {INSTANT, SORCERY}`\n  and `event.spell is not self`-cast-irrelevant. Effect: find a creature you control with\n  `power >= 1`; `controller.choose_yes_no(\"Casualty 1: sacrifice a creature to copy?\")`;\n  if yes, pick the creature (`choose_card`), `sacrifice(game, controller, creature)`,\n  then `game.stack.push(copy_spell(game, event.spell, controller,\n  new_targets=event.spell.targets))`.\n- **Edge cases:** `copy_spell` *returns* a `StackObject` but does NOT push it — you must\n  `game.stack.push(...)` the result yourself. Pushing it puts the copy on top of the\n  original so it resolves first. No eligible creature → no offer; the dragon itself can be\n  the sacrifice. Don't offer casualty for the dragon's own spell (it's a creature, not I/S).\n\n### sos_245 — Witherbloom, the Balancer `{6}{B}{G}` 5/5 Elder Dragon (complex)\n- **Clauses:** Affinity for creatures (self, {1} less per creature you control). Flying,\n  deathtouch. \"Instant and sorcery spells you cast have affinity for creatures.\"\n- **FDN analogue:** `cards/fdn/fdn_6` (ClawsOut) for affinity-as-`cost_reduction`.\n- **Seams:** `keywords=Keyword.FLYING|Keyword.DEATHTOUCH`.\n  Own affinity: override `cost_reduction(game)` = count creatures `self.controller`\n  controls (battlefield, `CardType.CREATURE in card_types`). Granting affinity to your\n  I/S spells: implement `external_cost_reduction(self, game, card, controller)` returning\n  the creature count when `controller is self.controller` and\n  `card.card_types & {INSTANT, SORCERY}`, else 0. **Requires gap \"external cost\n  reduction\".**\n- **Edge cases:** while Witherbloom is on the stack (being cast), it's not yet a creature\n  you control — its own affinity counts other creatures only (battlefield query naturally\n  excludes the stack). Clamp handled by `get_cost_reduction`. Don't double-count if both\n  self `cost_reduction` and external apply (they apply to different cards).\n\n### sos_4 — Together as One `{6}` Sorcery (complex)\n- **Clauses:** Converge — target player draws X, deals X damage to any target, you gain X\n  life; X = number of colors of mana spent to cast this spell.\n- **FDN analogue:** `cards/fdn/fdn_205` (colors_spent). Targeting like `fdn_48`.\n- **Seams:** `Sorcery`. `get_targets`: two `TargetRequirement`s — (1) a player (zone\n  BATTLEFIELD or however players are targeted; use a player filter), (2) \"any target\"\n  (creature OR player; filter accepts objects with `damage_marked` or `life`).\n  `on_resolve`: compute `cs = self.colors_spent`; `X = len(cs) if isinstance(cs, list)\n  else int(cs or 0)` (engine sets a list; FDN test convention uses int — handle both).\n  Then `draw_card` X times for chosen player; `deal_damage(game, self, any_target, X)`;\n  `self.controller.life += X`.\n- **Edge cases:** X=0 when only generic/no colored mana spent → all three sub-effects are\n  no-ops (loops run 0 times, deal_damage(≤0) returns early). Order: draw, then damage,\n  then life (as printed). Damage target may be the same player who draws.\n\n### sos_57 — Mana Sculpt `{1}{U}{U}` Instant (medium)\n- **Clauses:** Counter target spell. If you control a Wizard, add {C} equal to the amount\n  of mana spent to cast that spell at the beginning of your next main phase.\n- **FDN analogue:** `cards/fdn/fdn_48` (Refute) for counter-target-spell\n  (`can_cast`/`get_targets` over `game.stack.objects()`, `_counter_spell` helper).\n- **Seams:** `Instant`. Copy the `_counter_spell` / `_get_chosen_target` helpers pattern\n  from fdn_48. In `on_resolve`: capture `countered = target.source` and\n  `spent = getattr(countered, \"mana_spent\", 0)` **before** countering (needs gap\n  \"amount of mana spent\"). Counter the spell. If `self.controller` controls a Wizard\n  (`\"Wizard\" in obj.subtypes` on battlefield), register a one-shot\n  `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` trigger (needs gap \"beginning-of-main-phase\n  event\") whose condition is `event.player is self.controller`; effect adds\n  `ManaType.COLORLESS` × `spent` to the controller's pool and then unregisters itself\n  (`game.trigger_manager.unregister(marker_source)`).\n- **Edge cases:** no Wizard → no delayed mana. \"next main phase\" = first main phase of\n  either player where the controller is active; one-shot (unregister after firing). If the\n  countered spell was itself free-cast, `mana_spent` is 0 → adds nothing.\n\n### sos_1 — The Dawning Archaic `{10}` 7/7 Legendary Avatar (complex)\n- **Clauses:** Costs {1} less per instant/sorcery card in your graveyard. Reach. \"Whenever\n  this attacks, you may cast target I/S from your graveyard without paying its mana cost.\n  If that spell would be put into your graveyard, exile it instead.\"\n- **FDN analogue:** `cards/fdn/fdn_167` (Tolarian Terror) for the graveyard-count\n  `cost_reduction`. `cast_spell_free` for the free cast.\n- **Seams:** `Creature(keywords=Keyword.REACH, base_power=7, base_toughness=7,\n  supertypes={Supertype.LEGENDARY})`. `cost_reduction(game)`: count I/S in\n  `self.controller` graveyard (copy fdn_167). `register_triggers`: register an\n  `AttacksTriggeredEvent` trigger (needs gap \"attacks triggers fire\"); condition\n  `event.creature is self`. Effect: gather I/S cards in controller's graveyard; if any and\n  `choose_yes_no`, pick one (`choose_card`), register a card-specific\n  `MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent` replacement that redirects *that card* to exile\n  (set `destination=\"exile\"`), then `cast_spell_free(game, controller, chosen,\n  Zone.GRAVEYARD)`.\n- **Edge cases:** empty graveyard → no trigger effect. The exile-redirect replacement must\n  match only the chosen card (filter by identity) and be self-unregistering after it fires\n  once. Reach is purely a blocking keyword (already handled in `combat._can_block`). The\n  cost reduction only reduces generic (the whole cost is generic {10}).\n\n### sos_13 — Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares `{1}{W}{W} // {W}` (complex)\n- **Clauses:** Front: Creature — Cat Cleric, 3/3 white. ETB: target player creates a 1/1\n  W/B Inkling token with flying; then if an opponent controls more creatures than you,\n  this creature becomes *prepared*. While prepared, you may cast a copy of its spell\n  (Swords to Plowshares: exile target creature, its controller gains life = its power);\n  casting the copy unprepares it.\n- **FDN analogue:** ETB token creation like `create_token`; activated-ability gating like\n  `cards/fdn/fdn_91` (Kellan) state-flag pattern; targeting like fdn_48.\n- **Seams:** `Creature` front class (the canonical class in this file). Set `self.is_prepared\n  = False` in `__init__`. `register_triggers`: ETB trigger (`EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent`,\n  condition `event.permanent is self`). Effect: choose target player, `create_token` a 1/1\n  flier (`Creature(name=\"Inkling\", base_power=1, base_toughness=1, keywords=Keyword.FLYING)`,\n  colors W/B noted in rules_text); then count creatures: if `opp_creatures > my_creatures`,\n  `self.is_prepared = True`. `get_activated_abilities`: one ability available only when\n  `self.is_prepared` (cost returns False otherwise) — sorcery-speed copy-of-spell:\n  put a Swords effect on the stack (choose target creature; `exile(game, creature)`; that\n  creature's controller `.life += power`), then set `self.is_prepared = False`.\n- **Edge cases:** \"more creatures than you\" strictly greater; the token counts toward\n  *your* count only after it's created (it enters under the *target player*'s control —\n  if you targeted yourself it raises your count). Casting the copy when not prepared is\n  illegal (cost guard). Keep entire DFC behavior card-local; only ETB + targeting + token\n  + exile engine helpers are reused.\n\n### sos_120 — Improvisation Capstone `{5}{R}{R}` Sorcery — Lesson (complex)\n- **Clauses:** Exile from top of library until total MV ≥ 4; you may cast any number of\n  them for free. Paradigm: exile this spell; after you first resolve a spell with this\n  name, you may cast a copy of it from exile for free at the beginning of each of your\n  first main phases.\n- **FDN analogue:** `cast_spell_free` for the free casts; main-phase delayed trigger\n  (new event); MV via `ManaCost.cmc`.\n- **Seams:** `Sorcery`. `on_resolve`: from `self.controller` library top, move cards to\n  exile (`move_to_zone(... Zone.LIBRARY, Zone.EXILE)`) accumulating `cmc` until total ≥ 4;\n  for each exiled card that is castable, offer `choose_yes_no` then\n  `cast_spell_free(game, controller, c, Zone.EXILE)`. Paradigm: after resolving, exile\n  *this* card (the engine would send a sorcery to graveyard — override by moving self to\n  exile in `on_resolve`/via replacement) and register a repeating\n  `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` trigger (needs gap \"main-phase event\"), condition\n  `event.player is controller and event.is_precombat`, effect: offer to cast a copy of\n  this card from exile for free.\n- **Edge cases:** library runs out before reaching MV 4 → stop. Lands among exiled cards\n  can't be \"cast\" (skip — only cast spells). Paradigm copy is a *copy* (don't move the\n  exiled original; create a token-copy or re-castable copy). \"First resolve\" → register the\n  Paradigm trigger only once. This is the hardest part; Paradigm may be implemented after\n  the base spell works.\n\n### sos_201 — Lorehold, the Historian `{3}{R}{W}` 5/5 Elder Dragon (expert)\n- **Clauses:** Flying, haste. \"Each instant and sorcery card in your hand has miracle {2}.\"\n  \"At the beginning of each opponent's upkeep, you may discard a card; if you do, draw a\n  card.\"\n- **FDN analogue:** opponent-upkeep loot — `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent`/upkeep trigger\n  patterns (fdn_28 surveil shows draw-trigger + choose plumbing); miracle uses the new\n  `cast_with_alternative_cost`.\n- **Seams:** `keywords=Keyword.FLYING|Keyword.HASTE`. `register_triggers`: (a)\n  `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent` trigger (needs gap \"upkeep player field\"); condition\n  `event.player is not self.controller`; effect: `choose_yes_no` → if yes pick a card to\n  discard (`choose_card`), `discard`, then `draw_card`. (b) Miracle: register a\n  `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent` trigger; condition: `event.player is self.controller`, the\n  drawn `event.card` is I/S and owned by controller, and it is the first card drawn this\n  turn (`event.player.cards_drawn_this_turn == 1` — engine increments before firing).\n  Effect: `choose_yes_no(\"Cast for miracle {2}?\")`; if yes,\n  `cast_with_alternative_cost(game, controller, event.card, ManaCost(generic=2))`.\n- **Edge cases:** miracle only applies while Lorehold is on the battlefield and the card is\n  in *your* hand at draw time. Only the first draw of the turn qualifies. Opponent-upkeep\n  loot is \"may\" and only draws if you discarded. Haste lets the dragon attack the turn it\n  enters (engine already keys off `summoning_sick`+HASTE). Miracle is the hardest sub-part\n  — land the upkeep loot + keywords first.\n\n### sos_97 — Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer `{1}{B}{B}` Planeswalker, loyalty 3 (expert)\n- **Clauses:** +1 Surveil 2. −1 any number of target players each discard a card. −2\n  return target creature card MV ≤ 3 from your graveyard to the battlefield. −7 flip five\n  coins; target opponent skips their next X turns (X = heads).\n- **FDN analogue:** `cards/fdn/fdn_44` (Kaito) for `get_loyalty_abilities` + `_resolve_target`\n  pattern; `cards/fdn/fdn_28` for surveil; `cards/fdn/fdn_182` for graveyard→battlefield\n  return.\n- **Seams:** `Planeswalker(starting_loyalty=3, supertypes={Supertype.LEGENDARY},\n  subtypes={\"Ral\"})`. `get_loyalty_abilities` returns four `LoyaltyAbility`:\n  - `+1` Surveil 2: look at top 2 of controller's library, for each `choose_yes_no` to put\n    in graveyard (fdn_28 pattern extended to 2 cards).\n  - `−1`: for each target player (read from `pw._resolve_targets` list; default both / the\n    chosen subset), that player `choose_card`+`discard` one card.\n  - `−2`: read `pw._resolve_target` (a creature card in controller's graveyard with\n    `mana_cost.cmc <= 3`); remove from graveyard and put onto battlefield under\n    controller (`move_to_zone(... GRAVEYARD, BATTLEFIELD)` or graveyard.remove + bf.add +\n    register triggers, like fdn_182).\n  - `−7`: flip 5 coins (`random`), `heads = sum`; choose target opponent; set\n    `game.skipped_turns[opp_index] = game.skipped_turns.get(opp_index,0) + heads`\n    (needs gap \"skip turns\").\n- **Activation/tests:** loyalty abilities are activated by constructing\n  `LoyaltyAbilityInstance(source=pw, controller=ctrl, loyalty_cost=ab.loyalty_cost,\n  effect=ab.effect)` and calling `engine/abilities.activate_ability`; set `pw._resolve_target`\n  / `pw._resolve_targets` before activation (fdn_44 convention).\n- **Edge cases:** −2 filter must reject MV > 3 and non-creatures. −7 X can be 0 (no heads)\n  → no skip. Skip mechanic in a 2-player game means the opponent's queued turns are\n  consumed and the active player effectively takes consecutive turns; verify against the\n  `advance_phase` normal-branch loop. Loyalty cost can't drop below 0 (engine enforces).\n\n### sos_257 — Great Hall of the Biblioplex — Land (complex)\n- **Clauses:** `{T}: Add {C}`. `{T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color; spend only on\n  an I/S spell.` `{5}: If not already a creature, becomes a 2/4 Wizard creature with\n  \"Whenever you cast an I/S spell, this gets +1/+0 until end of turn\"; still a land.`\n- **FDN analogue:** `cards/fdn/fdn_141` (Giada) for `get_mana_abilities` (tap cost +\n  restricted-mana note); `cards/fdn/fdn_91` (Kellan) for the animate-via-activated-ability\n  mutation pattern; `cards/fdn/fdn_6` end-of-turn `ContinuousEffect` for the +1/+0.\n- **Seams:** `Land`. `get_mana_abilities`: (1) `{T}: Add {C}` — `cost` taps, `mana_produced`\n  adds `ManaType.COLORLESS`. (2) `{T}, Pay 1 life` — `cost` taps + `controller.life -= 1`;\n  `mana_produced` adds a chosen color. (The \"spend only on I/S\" restriction is a known\n  engine simplification — note it in rules_text; the mana pool has no restriction tags, so\n  model best-effort or document the gap.) `get_activated_abilities`: `{5}` ability — `cost`\n  pays `ManaCost(generic=5)` from pool; `effect`: if `CardType.CREATURE not in\n  self.card_types`, add CREATURE to `card_types`, set `subtypes |= {\"Wizard\"}`,\n  set `base_power`/`base_toughness`-style fields (note: `Land` is not a `Creature`, so the\n  implementer must attach `modified_power=2`/`modified_toughness=4` and the combat-required\n  attrs, or model the animated state carefully — simplest: give the Land the creature\n  attributes it needs: `base_power=2, base_toughness=4, modified_power=2,\n  modified_toughness=4, damage_marked=0, summoning_sick=...`, since combat eligibility keys\n  off `hasattr(c, \"base_power\")`). Register a `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` trigger (needs gap\n  \"spell-cast triggers fire\") that, while animated and `event.controller is self.controller`\n  and `event.card` is I/S, adds an end-of-turn `ContinuousEffect` (Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS /\n  SubLayer.MODIFY_PT) granting +1/+0.\n- **Edge cases:** `{5}` is idempotent if already a creature (guard on CREATURE in\n  card_types). The +1/+0 must be until end of turn (use `DURATION_END_OF_TURN`). Animating\n  doesn't remove LAND, and lands have summoning sickness for *attacking* but tapping for\n  mana is unaffected (the {T} mana abilities still work while animated). The\n  spell-cast +1/+0 trigger should only do anything while the land is currently a creature.\n\n---\n\n## Section 3 — Implementation order\n\nDo shared engine work first, then cards simplest→hardest. After each engine seam, run\n`pytest engine_tests` to confirm nothing regressed (especially after wiring\n`SpellCastTriggeredEvent`).\n\n**Group 0 — Shared engine seams (do first; unblocks everything).**\nRationale: every card below depends on at least one. Implement and regression-test in this\norder so failures are isolated:\n1. `external_cost_reduction` hook + `get_cost_reduction` aggregation (additive, low risk).\n2. `mana_spent` tracking (`ManaPool.last_payment_total` + set in `cast_spell`).\n3. `AttacksTriggeredEvent` firing in `declare_attackers_step`.\n4. `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent.player` field + pass active player.\n5. `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` new event + fire in `run_turn`.\n6. `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` firing in `cast_spell`/`cast_spell_free` (highest blast\n   radius — test immediately).\n7. `cast_with_alternative_cost` helper.\n8. `skipped_turns` + `advance_phase` skip loop.\n\n**Group 1 — Pure keyword / cost-reduction cards (simplest).**\nRationale: validate the engine seams with the least extra logic.\n- **sos_245 Witherbloom** (affinity self + external; Flying/Deathtouch keywords).\n- **sos_4 Together as One** (Converge via existing `colors_spent`; just targeting + math).\n\n**Group 2 — Single-mechanic cards.**\n- **sos_226 Silverquill** (casualty via spell-cast trigger + `copy_spell`).\n- **sos_57 Mana Sculpt** (counterspell via fdn_48 + delayed main-phase mana).\n- **sos_1 The Dawning Archaic** (graveyard cost-reduction + attacks trigger free-cast +\n  exile replacement).\n\n**Group 3 — Multi-clause permanents.**\n- **sos_257 Great Hall** (mana abilities + animate + spell-cast +1/+0 trigger).\n- **sos_13 Emeritus of Truce** (ETB token + prepared activated copy-spell).\n\n**Group 4 — Expert / multi-system (hardest, last).**\nRationale: each combines several seams and has the most edge cases.\n- **sos_97 Ral Zarek** (4 loyalty abilities incl. surveil, reanimation w/ MV filter, and\n  the skip-turns ultimate).\n- **sos_201 Lorehold** (opponent-upkeep loot via upkeep-player field + miracle via\n  `cast_with_alternative_cost` on the draw trigger).\n- **sos_120 Improvisation Capstone** (exile-until-MV free casts + Paradigm repeating\n  main-phase copy) — most novel control flow; finish last.\n\nFor each card: write `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py` covering the golden path + the listed\nedge cases, and run `pytest cards/sos/sos_<N>` plus the full `pytest` before moving on.\n","numLines":327,"startLine":1,"totalLines":327}}}
