{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - **Phase 2 of 2 — IMPLEMENTATION (TDD).** Implement 10 SOS cards: **1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257** in `/workspace/cards/sos/`. Each card directory has a `card_spec.json` (oracle text) and a `card_impl.py` template stub to fill in. Class must stay in `cards/sos/sos_<N>/card_impl.py`.\n   - Use completed FDN cards in `/workspace/cards/fdn/` as implementation examples; refer to `RULEBOOK.txt` for deep rules (via the `grep-rulebook` skill — never `cat`/Read it whole).\n   - Follow `/workspace/PLAN.md` (read in full): engine-gap analysis, per-card plans (nearest FDN analogue + exact seams), implementation order. If a point is wrong, correct course and note the deviation in PLAN.md.\n   - **Strict TDD**: vertical tracer-bullet, one failing test at a time through the engine's public interface (`test_utils`: create_game, set_board_state, cast_spell, advance_to_phase, declare_attackers, declare_blockers). Red → minimal green → repeat. Do NOT write all tests up front.\n   - Build shared engine seams FIRST, then cards simplest→hardest.\n   - **Discipline (verbatim intent):** Test the real engine, not a stand-in — never hand-construct internal events, pop the stack and call on_resolve() directly, or script a player's internal queue. Reuse before you add; mirror nearest FDN card; keep engine edits minimal/additive. Requirements (card_spec.json + RULEBOOK.txt) are the source of truth, not tests.\n   - **Guard the engine:** after each card and after any `engine/` change, run `python3 -m pytest engine_tests/ -q` — never ship a regression.\n   - Write `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py` per card covering golden path + edge cases.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - MTG engine: zones, LIFO stack, triggered abilities (TriggerManager.fire_event, APNAP, isinstance subtype matching), replacement effects (ReplacementManager.apply, \"instead\", prevented flag, destination redirection), 7-layer continuous effects (EffectManager.apply_all resets-then-reapplies, idempotent), state-based actions.\n   - Casting pipeline (engine/casting.py): cast_spell (timing → can_cast → hand→stack → choose targets → protection check → pay → on_cast → push StackObject with _resolve_spell on_resolve), cast_spell_free (no pay/timing, from any zone), _resolve_spell (sets card.chosen_targets then on_resolve, moves permanent→bf / non-permanent→graveyard).\n   - Keyword enum: FLYING, FIRST_STRIKE, DOUBLE_STRIKE, DEATHTOUCH, TRAMPLE, LIFELINK, VIGILANCE, REACH, HASTE, FLASH, DEFENDER, HEXPROOF, INDESTRUCTIBLE, MENACE, WARD, PROWESS. Surveil/Converge/Affinity/Prepared/Paradigm/Miracle/Casualty are card-logic mechanics, NOT keyword flags.\n   - ManaCost.cmc = generic + sum(pips) + len(hybrid). ManaCost is frozen dataclass.\n   - colors_spent set by cast_spell as `list(player.mana_pool.last_payment_colors)`. move_zone DELETES `colors_spent` on zone change (but NOT mana_spent). Converge cards (fdn_205) read colors_spent as int when tests set it directly (`self.colors_spent: int = 0` default; on_resolve does `range(count)`).\n   - TargetRequirement(filter_fn, description, zone). Triggered abilities have NO targeting step — effect(game) does its own choosing via controller.choose_*.\n   - Loyalty: LoyaltyAbility(loyalty_cost, effect, description) from get_loyalty_abilities(); activated via LoyaltyAbilityInstance(source, controller, loyalty_cost, effect) + activate_ability (sorcery-speed only, once-per-turn via module-level _loyalty_activated_this_turn, loyalty can't go <0). Effects read pw._resolve_target / pw._resolve_targets.\n   - ActivatedAbility cost signature is inconsistent across FDN: fdn_182/fdn_141 use `cost(game, src) -> bool`; fdn_91 uses `cost(game) -> bool`. ActivatedAbilityInstance.cost is called as `cost(game, source)`.\n   - copy_spell(game, original, controller, new_targets) returns a StackObject (does NOT push — caller must push). Binds _copy_resolve (no zone move).\n   - DeterministicPlayer pops scripted answers from a deque (_script) for all choose methods.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **/workspace/PLAN.md** — THE handoff. 8 seams (Section 1), per-card plans (Section 2), order (Section 3: seams in order 1-8, then Group1 sos_245+sos_4, Group2 sos_226+sos_57+sos_1, Group3 sos_257+sos_13, Group4 sos_97+sos_201+sos_120).\n   - **/workspace/AGENTS.md** — Hard rules: card class must stay in `cards/sos/{card_id}/card_impl.py`; **engine_tests/ is READ-ONLY (do not modify/add/delete)**; **never edit any `cards/fdn/fdn_*/tests.py`**; **additive-only engine edits — may add files/methods/classes/helpers and modify existing function bodies, but MUST NOT rename/move/delete anything existing in engine/**. SOS tests go at `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py`. Run `pytest` from workspace root; pytest.ini discovers test_*.py and tests.py with 5-min timeout.\n   - **engine/card.py** — CardImpl hooks (can_cast, cost_reduction→0, on_cast, on_resolve, get_targets, register_triggers, register_replacement_effects, get_activated_abilities, get_modes). Creature has base_power/base_toughness/modified_power/modified_toughness/power(property)/toughness(property)/damage_marked/is_tapped/summoning_sick(default True)/is_attacking/is_blocking/plus_one_counters/minus_one_counters/is_token/dealt_deathtouch_damage. _reset_characteristics resets card_types to _original_card_types + keywords (Creature also resets modified_power/toughness + counters + combat-restriction flags). Land.can_cast→False, get_mana_abilities()→[]. Planeswalker(starting_loyalty, ...) has loyalty/get_loyalty_abilities(). \n     **EDIT MADE:** Added `external_cost_reduction(self, game, card, controller) -> int: return 0` hook right after `cost_reduction`.\n   - **engine/casting.py** — get_cost_reduction (line ~89), cast_spell (push ~line 246), cast_spell_free (push ~line 371), _resolve_spell, _PERMANENT_TYPES frozenset, _apply_cost_reduction.\n     **EDIT 1 (get_cost_reduction):** after `card.controller = prev_controller`, added:\n     ```python\n     # Aggregate cost reductions granted by other permanents the controller controls\n     for obj in controller.zones[Zone.BATTLEFIELD].get_all():\n         hook = getattr(obj, \"external_cost_reduction\", None)\n         if callable(hook):\n             raw += hook(game, card, controller)\n     ```\n     **EDIT 2 (cast_spell, after colors_spent set):** added:\n     ```python\n     card.mana_spent = player.mana_pool.last_payment_total  # type: ignore[attr-defined]\n     ```\n   - **engine/mana.py** — ManaPool.pay computes _last_payment_colors; can_pay; _auto_pay_generic.\n     **EDIT 1:** __init__ added `self._last_payment_total: int = 0`.\n     **EDIT 2:** added `last_payment_total` property returning `self._last_payment_total`.\n     **EDIT 3:** in pay() commit section, replaced the colors loop with one that also sums total:\n     ```python\n     colors_spent: set[Color] = set()\n     total_spent = 0\n     for mt, old_amount in self._pool.items():\n         new_amount = working.get(mt, 0)\n         if new_amount < old_amount:\n             total_spent += old_amount - new_amount\n             if mt in _MANA_TO_COLOR:\n                 colors_spent.add(_MANA_TO_COLOR[mt])\n     self._last_payment_colors = sorted(colors_spent, key=lambda c: c.value)\n     self._last_payment_total = total_spent\n     self._pool = working\n     return True\n     ```\n   - **engine/combat.py** — declare_attackers_step: gathers eligible (`hasattr(c, \"base_power\") and _can_attack(c)`), active.choose(eligible, \"declare attackers\"), normalizes to list, validates, sets combat.attackers/attacker_blockers/is_attacking, taps unless VIGILANCE.\n     **EDIT MADE (most recent):** Inside the `for attacker in chosen` loop, after the tap block, added:\n     ```python\n     # Fire the \"whenever this creature attacks\" trigger.\n     from engine.events import AttacksTriggeredEvent\n     game.trigger_manager.fire_event(\n         game, AttacksTriggeredEvent(creature=attacker, attacker=attacker)\n     )\n     ```\n   - **engine/events.py** — SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell, player, card, controller) and AttacksTriggeredEvent(creature, attacker) ALREADY EXIST. BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent currently `pass` (NEEDS player field). MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent has mutable `destination` + `prevented`; subclasses CreatureDiesReplacementEvent/PermanentDestroyedReplacementEvent/SacrificeReplacementEvent expose `card` property. DrawsCardTriggeredEvent(player, card). No BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent yet.\n   - **engine/turn.py** — line 202-204 upkeep fires `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent()` (no-arg). Combat dispatch at line 207 (`elif game.phase == Phase.COMBAT and game.step is not None`). Cleanup at line 209. Main phases have step=None; priority_loop at line 214. NEEDS main-phase event branch.\n   - **engine/game_state.py** — __init__ has extra_turns=[], _normal_next_index=1. advance_phase normal branch (else after extra_turns, lines 156-158): `self.active_player_index = self._normal_next_index; self._normal_next_index = 1 - self._normal_next_index`. NEEDS skipped_turns dict + skip loop. `active_player` property, `non_active_player` = players[1 - active_player_index].\n   - **engine/stack.py** — StackObject(source, controller, targets, on_resolve, is_mana_ability). copy_spell shallow-copies source, binds _copy_resolve. Stack._items (index -1 = top), objects() returns top→bottom. priority_loop pops top + on_resolve + check_state_based_actions.\n   - **engine/triggers.py** — TriggerRegistration(event_type, condition(game,event)→bool|None, effect(game)→None, source, controller). register/unregister(source identity)/fire_event(APNAP — active controller's triggers first/bottom).\n   - **engine/abilities.py** — activate_ability dispatches LoyaltyAbilityInstance (sorcery-speed, once-per-turn, loyalty≥0) vs ActivatedAbilityInstance (cost(game,source)→bool; mana abilities resolve immediately, else push StackObject). tap_cost(game, source) helper. clear_loyalty_tracking().\n   - **engine/zones.py** — move_zone deletes obj.colors_spent on change. move_to_zone(game, card, from_zone, to_zone, replacement_event=None): consults replacement on leaving battlefield, fires LeavesBattlefield/CreatureDies, unregisters; on entering battlefield fires ETB then register_triggers/register_replacement_effects. _DESTINATION_ZONE_MAP maps \"exile\"/\"graveyard\"/\"hand\"/\"library\".\n   - **engine/game.py** — helpers: deal_damage (≤0 returns early, fires DealsDamage/LosesLife, lifelink), destroy (skips INDESTRUCTIBLE), sacrifice, exile (finds zone), draw_card (sets cards_drawn_this_turn lazily, fires DrawsCardTriggeredEvent, sets drawn_from_empty_library if empty), discard, create_token (sets is_token/owner/controller, adds to bf, fires ETB, registers triggers), add_counter/remove_counter, tap/untap. run_game loop.\n   - **engine/continuous_effects.py** — ContinuousEffect(source, layer, sublayer, apply, timestamp, duration). Layer.TYPE=4, ABILITY=6, POWER_TOUGHNESS=7. SubLayer.SET_PT=\"7b\", MODIFY_PT=\"7c\". DURATION_END_OF_TURN=0, DURATION_PERMANENT=-1. apply_all resets battlefield objects then applies in layer/sublayer/timestamp order. EffectManager.add auto-assigns timestamp.\n   - **engine/replacement_effects.py** — ReplacementEffect(event_type, source, condition, replacement(game,event)→event, controller). apply collects matching (isinstance), each applies once, returns modified event.\n   - **test_utils.py** — cast_spell: finds card by name in hand, sets sorcery timing for non-instants (sets active/priority index + PRECOMBAT_MAIN if needed), REQUIRES empty stack, scripts targets via `player._script.appendleft` in reverse, calls engine cast_spell, then _resolve_top_of_stack (pops + on_resolve + SBAs in a loop