{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - **Phase 2 of 2 — IMPLEMENTATION (TDD).** Implement 10 SOS cards: **1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257** in `/workspace/cards/sos/`. Each card directory has `card_spec.json` (oracle text, source of truth) and a `card_impl.py` template stub. Class must stay in `cards/sos/sos_<N>/card_impl.py`.\n   - Use completed FDN cards in `/workspace/cards/fdn/` as implementation examples; refer to `RULEBOOK.txt` only via the `grep-rulebook` skill (never cat/Read whole).\n   - Follow `/workspace/PLAN.md` (the entire self-contained handoff): 8 engine seams (Section 1), per-card plans (Section 2), implementation order (Section 3). If a point is wrong, correct course and note the deviation in PLAN.md.\n   - **Strict TDD**: vertical tracer-bullet, one failing test at a time through the engine's public interface (test_utils: create_game, set_board_state, cast_spell, advance_to_phase, declare_attackers, declare_blockers). Red → minimal green → repeat. Do NOT write all tests up front. Build shared engine seams FIRST, then cards simplest→hardest.\n   - **Discipline (verbatim intent):** \"Test the real engine, not a stand-in — never hand-construct internal events, pop the stack and call on_resolve() directly, or script a player's internal queue.\" \"Reuse before you add; mirror nearest FDN card; keep engine edits minimal/additive.\" \"Requirements (card_spec.json + RULEBOOK.txt) are the source of truth, not tests.\"\n   - **Guard the engine:** after each card and after any engine/ change, run `python3 -m pytest engine_tests/ -q` — never ship a regression.\n   - Write `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py` per card covering golden path + edge cases; run `pytest cards/sos/sos_<N>` plus the full `pytest` before moving on.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - MTG engine: zones, LIFO stack, triggered abilities (APNAP), replacement effects, 7-layer continuous effects, state-based actions.\n   - **fire_event (engine/triggers.py) does NOT run effects immediately** — it pushes matching triggers as StackObjects (on_resolve=trigger.effect) onto the stack, resolved later by priority_loop or test_utils._resolve_top_of_stack. The **effect callable receives only `game`, NOT the event** — so to access event data (e.g. event.spell) in an effect, stash it on a known object in the condition callable (which receives `(game, event)`).\n   - **TriggerRegistration(event_type, condition(game,event)→bool|None, effect(game)→None, source, controller)**; register/unregister(source identity)/get_triggers/clear.\n   - **set_board_state bypasses ETB** (directly adds to zone containers, sets owner/controller). To get triggers registered the real way, use `move_to_zone(game, card, Zone.HAND, Zone.BATTLEFIELD)` (fires ETB + calls register_triggers + register_replacement_effects).\n   - **test_utils.cast_spell requires an empty stack** (raises TestSetupError otherwise) — so counterspell tests must call `engine.casting.cast_spell` directly to put a spell on the stack and respond to it; resolve via `test_utils._resolve_top_of_stack(game)` (pops + on_resolve + SBAs).\n   - **Mana pools empty on every phase/step transition** (advance_phase calls empty_mana_pools). advance_to_phase only calls advance_phase (does NOT fire main-phase events — those fire in turn.run_turn). run_turn runs a FULL turn, so delayed mana added at a main phase is emptied before observable. Delayed-mana triggers are therefore tested by driving the event through `game.trigger_manager.fire_event(...)` + `_resolve_top_of_stack`.\n   - ManaCost frozen dataclass; .cmc = generic + sum(pips) + len(hybrid). Color enum vs ManaType. ManaType.COLORLESS.\n   - cast_spell sets `card.colors_spent = list(player.mana_pool.last_payment_colors)` and `card.mana_spent = player.mana_pool.last_payment_total`. Converge cards default `self.colors_spent: int = 0` and handle both int (test) and list (real cast): `X = len(cs) if isinstance(cs, list) else int(cs or 0)`.\n   - copy_spell(game, original, controller, new_targets) returns a StackObject (does NOT push; caller must `game.stack.push(...)`); binds _copy_resolve (no zone move).\n   - get_cost_reduction aggregates `card.cost_reduction(game)` + sum of `obj.external_cost_reduction(game, card, controller)` over controller's battlefield, clamped to generic.\n   - TargetRequirement(filter_fn, description, zone); zone is metadata only (not enforced for DeterministicPlayer which just pops _script). Players are targeted with filter `hasattr(o, \"life\")`; \"any target\" = `hasattr(o, \"life\") or hasattr(o, \"damage_marked\")`.\n   - DeterministicPlayer: choose/choose_target/choose_yes_no/choose_card all pop from `self._script` (deque). create_game(scripts=(s1, s2)) seeds scripts. test_utils.cast_spell appendlefts targets in reverse.\n   - Keyword Flag enum: `Keyword.FLYING in card.keywords` works (Python 3.11). Supertype.LEGENDARY. CardType.{CREATURE,INSTANT,SORCERY,...}.\n   - deal_damage(game, source, target, amount): ≤0 returns early; player target reduces life; creature target adds damage_marked; fires triggers; lifelink. draw_card draws top of library (index -1), increments cards_drawn_this_turn, fires DrawsCardTriggeredEvent. sacrifice(game, player, permanent). create_token(game, player, token).\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **/workspace/PLAN.md** — read in full this session. 8 seams (Section 1 table), per-card plans (Section 2), order (Section 3: Group 0 seams 1-8; Group 1 sos_245+sos_4; Group 2 sos_226+sos_57+sos_1; Group 3 sos_257+sos_13; Group 4 sos_97+sos_201+sos_120). Confirms seam 7 (cast_with_alternative_cost) is for sos_201 miracle.\n   - **/workspace/AGENTS.md** — Hard rules (binding): card class stays in `cards/sos/{card_id}/card_impl.py`; **engine_tests/ READ-ONLY