redirect. Key finding: `_resolve_spell` moves I/S to graveyard via `move_to_zone(game, card, Zone.STACK, Zone.GRAVEYARD)` with NO replacement_event passed — meaning a standard `MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent`-based replacement registered via register_replacement_effects may NOT be consulted on spell resolution (since move_to_zone only consults replacements when leaving the battlefield and when a replacement_event is supplied). This needs verification before implementing the exile redirect.\n   PLAN's sos_1 plan: `Creature(keywords=Keyword.REACH, base_power=7, base_toughness=7, supertypes={Supertype.LEGENDARY})`, subtypes {\"Avatar\"}, mana_cost {10}; cost_reduction counts I/S in controller graveyard; register_triggers registers AttacksTriggeredEvent (condition event.creature is self); effect: gather I/S in controller graveyard, if any and choose_yes_no, choose_card, register a card-specific replacement redirecting THAT card to exile (destination=\"exile\", self-unregistering after firing once), then `cast_spell_free(game, controller, chosen, Zone.GRAVEYARD)`. Edge cases: empty graveyard → no effect; exile-redirect matches only chosen card by identity.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Continue implementing **sos_1 The Dawning Archaic** (task #6) per PLAN Section 2. First verify (via reading engine/replacement_effects.py and the rest of move_to_zone) whether the \"exile instead of graveyard\" redirect can use a registered ReplacementEffect on the spell resolution path (given _resolve_spell calls move_to_zone WITHOUT a replacement_event), or whether the chosen card needs its own card-level mechanism (e.g., the chosen I/S card overrides its graveyard destination, or the free-cast wraps the resolution). Then: write `cards/sos/sos_1/tests.py` starting with a failing properties test (name, {10}, 7/7, REACH, Legendary), implement the constructor (green), then add cost_reduction test (cast with reduced mana given N I/S in graveyard), then the attacks-trigger free-cast test (use declare_attackers to fire AttacksTriggeredEvent via the real engine since seam 3 fires it in declare_attackers_step), then the exile-redirect test. Per PLAN order, after sos_1 proceed to Group 3 (sos_257, sos_13), then Group 4 (sos_97, sos_201, sos_120). After each card run `python3 -m pytest cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py -q` and the full `python3 -m pytest -q` (currently 1215 passed) to guard against regressions.\n   Direct quote from PLAN sos_1 plan: \"`register_triggers`: register an `AttacksTriggeredEvent` trigger (needs gap \"attacks triggers fire\"); condition `event.creature is self`. Effect: gather I/S cards in controller's graveyard; if any and `choose_yes_no`, pick one (`choose_card`), register a card-specific `MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent` replacement that redirects *that card* to exile (set `destination=\"exile\"`), then `cast_spell_free(game, controller, chosen, Zone.GRAVEYARD)`.\"\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /home/node/.claude/projects/-workspace/ccba73e9-54b6-4808-89ce-87e442914ff8.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ccba73e9-54b6-4808-89ce-87e442914ff8","uuid":"3ad485e3-f309-42df-a44f-397fbe5ef35b","timestamp":"2026-06-04T07:51:08.506Z","isSynthetic":true}
