{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PDB2An8aa81NazQdGtNHNy","type":"tool_result","content":"250\t    (needs gap \"skip turns\").\n251\t- **Activation/tests:** loyalty abilities are activated by constructing\n252\t  `LoyaltyAbilityInstance(source=pw, controller=ctrl, loyalty_cost=ab.loyalty_cost,\n253\t  effect=ab.effect)` and calling `engine/abilities.activate_ability`; set `pw._resolve_target`\n254\t  / `pw._resolve_targets` before activation (fdn_44 convention).\n255\t- **Edge cases:** −2 filter must reject MV > 3 and non-creatures. −7 X can be 0 (no heads)\n256\t  → no skip. Skip mechanic in a 2-player game means the opponent's queued turns are\n257\t  consumed and the active player effectively takes consecutive turns; verify against the\n258\t  `advance_phase` normal-branch loop. Loyalty cost can't drop below 0 (engine enforces).\n259\t\n260\t### sos_257 — Great Hall of the Biblioplex — Land (complex)\n261\t- **Clauses:** `{T}: Add {C}`. `{T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color; spend only on\n262\t  an I/S spell.` `{5}: If not already a creature, becomes a 2/4 Wizard creature with\n263\t  \"Whenever you cast an I/S spell, this gets +1/+0 until end of turn\"; still a land.`\n264\t- **FDN analogue:** `cards/fdn/fdn_141` (Giada) for `get_mana_abilities` (tap cost +\n265\t  restricted-mana note); `cards/fdn/fdn_91` (Kellan) for the animate-via-activated-ability\n266\t  mutation pattern; `cards/fdn/fdn_6` end-of-turn `ContinuousEffect` for the +1/+0.\n267\t- **Seams:** `Land`. `get_mana_abilities`: (1) `{T}: Add {C}` — `cost` taps, `mana_produced`\n268\t  adds `ManaType.COLORLESS`. (2) `{T}, Pay 1 life` — `cost` taps + `controller.life -= 1`;\n269\t  `mana_produced` adds a chosen color. (The \"spend only on I/S\" restriction is a known\n270\t  engine simplification — note it in rules_text; the mana pool has no restriction tags, so\n271\t  model best-effort or document the gap.) `get_activated_abilities`: `{5}` ability — `cost`\n272\t  pays `ManaCost(generic=5)` from pool; `effect`: if `CardType.CREATURE not in\n273\t  self.card_types`, add CREATURE to `card_types`, set `subtypes |= {\"Wizard\"}`,\n274\t  set `base_power`/`base_toughness`-style fields (note: `Land` is not a `Creature`, so the\n275\t  implementer must attach `modified_power=2`/`modified_toughness=4` and the combat-required\n276\t  attrs, or model the animated state carefully — simplest: give the Land the creature\n277\t  attributes it needs: `base_power=2, base_toughness=4, modified_power=2,\n278\t  modified_toughness=4, damage_marked=0, summoning_sick=...`, since combat eligibility keys\n279\t  off `hasattr(c, \"base_power\")`). Register a `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` trigger (needs gap\n280\t  \"spell-cast triggers fire\") that, while animated and `event.controller is self.controller`\n281\t  and `event.card` is I/S, adds an end-of-turn `ContinuousEffect` (Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS /\n282\t  SubLayer.MODIFY_PT) granting +1/+0.\n283\t- **Edge cases:** `{5}` is idempotent if already a creature (guard on CREATURE in\n284\t  card_types). The +1/+0 must be until end of turn (use `DURATION_END_OF_TURN`). Animating\n285\t  doesn't remove LAND, and lands have summoning sickness for *attacking* but tapping for\n286\t  mana is unaffected (the {T} mana abilities still work while animated). The\n287\t  spell-cast +1/+0 trigger should only do anything while the land is currently a creature.\n288\t\n289\t---"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ccba73e9-54b6-4808-89ce-87e442914ff8","uuid":"a9660c10-17c9-4ba1-983e-c358083262c6","timestamp":"2026-06-04T07:58:49.237Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/PLAN.md","content":"    (needs gap \"skip turns\").\n- **Activation/tests:** loyalty abilities are activated by constructing\n  `LoyaltyAbilityInstance(source=pw, controller=ctrl, loyalty_cost=ab.loyalty_cost,\n  effect=ab.effect)` and calling `engine/abilities.activate_ability`; set `pw._resolve_target`\n  /