{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - **Phase 2 of 2 — IMPLEMENTATION (TDD).** Implement 10 SOS cards: **1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257** in `/workspace/cards/sos/`. Each card directory has `card_spec.json` (oracle text, source of truth) and a `card_impl.py` template stub. Class must stay in `cards/sos/sos_<N>/card_impl.py`.\n   - Use completed FDN cards in `/workspace/cards/fdn/` as implementation examples; refer to `RULEBOOK.txt` only via the `grep-rulebook` skill (never cat/Read whole).\n   - Follow `/workspace/PLAN.md` (the entire self-contained handoff): 8 engine seams (Section 1), per-card plans (Section 2), implementation order (Section 3). If a point is wrong, correct course and note the deviation in PLAN.md.\n   - **Strict TDD**: vertical tracer-bullet, one failing test at a time through the engine's public interface (test_utils: create_game, set_board_state, cast_spell, advance_to_phase, declare_attackers, declare_blockers). Red → minimal green → repeat. Do NOT write all tests up front. Build shared engine seams FIRST, then cards simplest→hardest.\n   - **Discipline (verbatim intent):** \"Test the real engine, not a stand-in — never hand-construct internal events, pop the stack and call on_resolve() directly, or script a player's internal queue.\" \"Reuse before you add; mirror nearest FDN card; keep engine edits minimal/additive.\" \"Requirements (card_spec.json + RULEBOOK.txt) are the source of truth, not tests.\"\n   - **Guard the engine:** after each card and after any engine/ change, run `python3 -m pytest engine_tests/ -q` — never ship a regression.\n   - Write `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py` per card covering golden path + edge cases; run `pytest cards/sos/sos_<N>` plus the full `pytest` before moving on.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - MTG engine: zones, LIFO stack, triggered abilities (APNAP), replacement effects, 7-layer continuous effects, state-based actions.\n   - **fire_event (engine/triggers.py) pushes matching triggers as StackObjects (on_resolve=trigger.effect); does NOT run effects immediately.** The effect callable receives only `game`; to access event data, stash it on a known object in the condition callable (which receives `(game, event)`).\n   - **TriggerRegistration(event_type, condition(game,event)→bool, effect(game)→None, source, controller)**.\n   - **ReplacementEffect(event_type, source, condition(game,event)→bool|None, replacement(game,event)→event, controller)**; ReplacementManager.register/unregister(source identity)/apply. apply uses `isinstance(event, effect.event_type)` so a parent-registered replacement matches subtype events. unregister removes ALL effects with `source is X`.\n   - **`move_to_zone(game, card, from_zone, to_zone, *, replacement_event=None)`** consults replacement effects ONLY when `replacement_event is not None AND from_zone == Zone.BATTLEFIELD`. On entering battlefield: fires ETB event, then calls register_triggers + register_replacement_effects. On leaving: fires LeavesBattlefield/CreatureDies, then unregisters. `move_zone` deletes `colors_spent` attr on move; `move_to_zone` uses owner's zone for non-battlefield source.\n   - **`_resolve_spell` (engine/casting.py)** sets `card.chosen_targets`, calls on_resolve; permanents → move_to_zone STACK→BATTLEFIELD; I/S → (now, after this session's edit) consults replacements then moves STACK→dest.\n   - **set_board_state bypasses ETB** (directly adds to zone containers, sets owner/controller). To register triggers the real way, use `move_to_zone(game, card, Zone.HAND, Zone.BATTLEFIELD)`.\n   - **test_utils.cast_spell requires empty stack** (raises TestSetupError otherwise) and wraps any cast exception (e.g. CastingError) in TestSetupError. Counterspell tests use `engine.casting.cast_spell` directly + `_resolve_top_of_stack`.\n   - **DeterministicPlayer** (engine/player.py): choose/choose_target/choose_yes_no/choose_card/assign_damage_order all `popleft()` from `self._script` (deque); ScriptExhaustedError when empty. create_game(scripts=(s1,s2)). test_utils.cast_spell appendlefts targets in reverse; declare_attackers appendlefts the attackers list; both consumed first via popleft.\n   - **declare_attackers_step (engine/combat.py)** fires `AttacksTriggeredEvent(creature=attacker, attacker=attacker)` for each attacker (after tap/is_attacking), via fire_event (pushes, doesn't resolve). `_can_attack` checks is_tapped, _cant_attack, DEFENDER, summoning_sick (unless HASTE). Combat eligibility keys off `hasattr(c, \"base_power\")`.\n   - **Two distinct ContinuousEffect classes**: `engine.card.ContinuousEffect` (apply/remove/description) vs `engine.continuous_effects.ContinuousEffect` (source, layer, sublayer, apply, timestamp, duration). P/T buffs use the latter.\n   - **EffectManager.apply_all** calls `_reset_objects` → `_reset_characteristics()` on every battlefield object, then applies sorted effects. apply_all is invoked ONLY in turn.py (133-136); NOT in resolve_state_based_actions. **Tests must call `game.effect_manager.apply_all(game)` manually** to make continuous effects visible. DURATION_END_OF_TURN=0 (swept by remove_expired), DURATION_PERMANENT=-1. Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS=7, SubLayer.MODIFY_PT=\"7c\", Layer.TYPE=4.\n   - **CardImpl._reset_characteristics** resets card_types→_original and keywords→_original (NOT subtypes, NOT modified_power). Creature._reset_characteristics also resets modified_power/toughness and counters.\n   - **State-based actions** (engine/state_based_actions.py): `_sba_creature_zero_toughness` destroys any battlefield obj where `hasattr(obj,\"toughness\") and obj.toughness <= 0`. CRITICAL constraint for animate-land cards.\n   - **ActivatedAbilityInstance(source, controller, cost, effect, is_mana_ability, description)**; cost called as `cost(game, source)→bool`, effect as `effect(game)`. `activate_ability(game, player, ability)`: mana abilities resolve immediately (effect called), regular abilities push StackObject(on_resolve=effect). Raises AbilityError if cost returns False. ManaAbility(cost, mana_produced, description). ActivatedAbility(cost, effect, description). card.get_mana_abilities()/get_activated_abilities() return these.\n   - `mana_pool.pay(ManaCost)` returns bool; `mana_pool.add(ManaType, n)`; `mana_pool.get(ManaType)`; `mana_pool.empty()`.\n   - ManaCost.parse(\"{10}\"), ManaCost() empty. ManaType.COLORLESS/WHITE/etc. CardType.{LAND,CREATURE,INSTANT,SORCERY}. Supertype.LEGENDARY. Keyword.REACH.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **/workspace/engine/events.py** — EDITED. Added new replacement subclass after SacrificeReplacementEvent:\n     ```python\n     @dataclass\n     class SpellToGraveyardReplacementEvent(MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent):\n         \"\"\"An instant/sorcery spell about to be put into a graveyard on resolution.\"\"\"\n         spell: Any = None\n         @property\n         def card(self) -> Any:\n             return self.spell\n     ```\n     (Base MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent has `destination=\"graveyard\"`, `controller`, `owner`, `prevented=False`, `card` property returns None. Existing subclasses: CreatureDiesReplacementEvent/PermanentDestroyedReplacementEvent/SacrificeReplacementEvent.)\n   - **/workspace/engine/casting.py** — EDITED `_resolve_spell` I/S branch (was `move_to_zone(game, card, Zone.STACK, Zone.GRAVEYARD)`):\n     ```python\n     else:\n         from engine.events import SpellToGraveyardReplacementEvent\n         from engine.zones import _DESTINATION_ZONE_MAP\n         owner = getattr(card, \"owner\", None) or player\n         repl = game.replacement_manager.apply(\n             game, SpellToGraveyardReplacementEvent(spell=card, controller=player, owner=owner))\n         if getattr(repl, \"prevented\", False):\n             stack_container = owner.zones[Zone.STACK]\n             if stack_container.contains(card):\n                 stack_container.remove(card)\n             return\n         dest = _DESTINATION_ZONE_MAP.get(getattr(repl, \"destination\", \"graveyard\"), Zone.GRAVEYARD)\n         move_to_zone(game, card, Zone.STACK, dest)\n     ```\n     No-op when nothing registered → spell goes to graveyard as before. cast_spell_free signature: `cast_spell_free(game, player, card, from_zone) -> None`. get_cost_reduction (89-116) sets card.controller=controller before calling cost_reduction, aggregates external_cost_reduction over battlefield, clamps to generic.\n   - **/workspace/cards/sos/sos_1/card_impl.py** — DONE. Full content:\n     ```python\n     def _instant_or_sorcery(card): return bool(getattr(card,\"card_types\",set()) & {CardType.INSTANT, CardType.SORCERY})\n     class TheDawningArchaic(Creature):\n         # {10} 7/7 Legendary {\"Avatar\"} Keyword.REACH\n         def cost_reduction(self, game):\n             controller = self.controller\n             if controller is None: return 0\n             return sum(1 for c in controller.zones[Zone.GRAVEYARD].get_all() if _instant_or_sorcery(c))\n         def register_triggers(self, game):\n             # registers AttacksTriggeredEvent, condition event.creature is source\n             # effect: candidates = I/S in controller graveyard; if none return;\n             #   if not controller.choose_yes_no(...): return\n             #   chosen = controller.choose_card(candidates, ...); if None return\n             #   marker = type(\"ArchaicExileRedirect\",(),{\"name\":...})()\n             #   register ReplacementEffect(event_type=MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent, source=marker,\n             #     condition=lambda g,e: e.card is chosen,\n             #     replacement=lambda g,e: (setattr(e,\"destination\",\"exile\"), game.replacement_manager.unregister(marker), e)[-1])\n             #   cast_spell_free(game, controller, chosen, Zone.GRAVEYARD)\n     ```\n   - **/workspace/cards/sos/sos_1/tests.py** — DONE (10 tests passing). Local `_Spark(Instant)` {R} no-op resolve, `_sorcery`/`_instant` helpers. Imports `from test_utils import TestSetupError as _TestSetupError` (aliased to avoid pytest collection warning). Tests: properties (name, {10}, 7/7, REACH, Legendary+Creature); cost reduction (3 I/S in graveyard → casts with {7}; empty graveyard + 7 mana → raises (CastingError, _TestSetupError)); attack trigger (`_attack` helper: move_to_zone HAND→BATTLEFIELD, set summoning_sick=False, declare_attackers([\"The Dawning Archaic\"]), _resolve_top_of_stack) — free-casts+exiles spell (scripts=([True, spark],[])); decline (scripts=([False],[]) → stays in graveyard); no-I/S (creature in graveyard, scripts=([],[]) → stays, stack empty).\n   - **/workspace/cards/sos/sos_257/card_impl.py** — DONE (written, NOT yet tested). `GreatHallOfTheBiblioplex(Land)`. Key elements:\n     ```python\n     class GreatHallOfTheBiblioplex(Land):\n         def __init__(self, **kwargs): ...; super().__init__(**kwargs); self._animated = False\n         @property\n         def power(self):\n             if not self._animated: raise AttributeError(\"power\")\n             return self.modified_power + self.plus_one_counters - self.minus_one_counters\n         @property\n         def toughness(self):\n             if not self._animated: raise AttributeError(\"toughness\")\n             return self.modified_toughness + self.plus_one_counters - self.minus_one_counters\n         def _animate(self):\n             self._animated = True\n             self.card_types = set(self.card_types) | {CardType.CREATURE}\n             self.subtypes = set(self.subtypes) | {\"Wizard\"}\n             self.base_power=2; self.base_toughness=4; self.modified_power=2; self.modified_toughness=4\n             self.plus_one_counters=0; self.minus_one_counters=0; self._base_plus_one_counters=0\n             self._base_minus_one_counters=0; self.damage_marked=0; self.is_attacking=False\n             self.is_blocking=False; self.is_token=False; self.dealt_deathtouch_damage=False\n             self.summoning_sick=False\n         def _reset_characteristics(self):\n             super()._reset_characteristics()\n             if self._animated:\n                 self.card_types = set(self.card_types) | {CardType.CREATURE}\n                 self.subtypes = set(self.subtypes) | {\"Wizard\"}\n                 self.modified_power=self.base_power; self.modified_toughness=self.base_toughness\n                 self.plus_one_counters=self._base_plus_one_counters\n                 self.minus_one_counters=self._base_minus_one_counters\n         def get_mana_abilities(self):  # ManaAbility {T}:Add{C}; ManaAbility {T},Pay1life:Add any color\n             # _cost_tap(game,src): if tapped False; tap; True. _produce_colorless(game): add COLORLESS 1.\n             # _cost_tap_life(game,src): if tapped/no ctrl False; tap; ctrl.life-=1; True.\n             # _produce_any(game): color=ctrl.choose(list(_COLORS),...); ctrl.mana_pool.add(color,1)\n         def get_activated_abilities(self):  # ActivatedAbility {5}\n             # _cost(game,src): ctrl.mana_pool.pay(ManaCost.parse(\"{5}\")). _effect(game): if CREATURE in card_types return; source._animate()\n         def register_triggers(self, game):  # SpellCastTriggeredEvent\n             # condition: source._animated and event.controller is source.controller and _instant_or_sorcery(event.card)\n             # effect: game.effect_manager.add(ContinuousEffect(source, Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS, SubLayer.MODIFY_PT, apply=lambda g: source.modified_power+=1 if animated, duration=DURATION_END_OF_TURN))\n     ```\n     `_COLORS = (WHITE, BLUE, BLACK, RED, GREEN)`. The \"spend only on I/S\" restriction documented as known engine simplification.\n   - **/workspace/cards/sos/sos_257/tests.py** — JUST WRITTEN (NOT yet run). 11 tests in 5 classes. Helpers: `_sorcery(name)` → Sorcery {1}; `_mana_instance(hall, player, index)` and `_animate_instance(hall, player)` build ActivatedAbilityInstance. Imports `from engine.abilities import AbilityError, ActivatedAbilityInstance, activate_ability`. Tests: TestGreatHallProperties (name; is land not creature; no power/toughness/base_power before animation via `not hasattr`); TestGreatHallManaAbilities (tap for colorless; tap+pay-1-life for any color with scripts=([ManaType.RED],[]); tapped land raises AbilityError); TestGreatHallAnimate (becomes 2/4 Wizard still land; idempotent while creature); TestGreatHallSpellCastBuff (`_battlefield_with_triggers` helper does set_board_state hand + move_to_zone; +1/+0 on I/S cast while animated → power==3 after apply_all; no buff when not animated → not hasattr power, no effect with source is hall).\n   - **/workspace/PLAN.md** — EDITED. Added a \"DEVIATION (implemented)\" note under the sos_1 section documenting the SpellToGraveyardReplacementEvent seam wiring replacements into _resolve_spell.\n   - **REFERENCE files read:** fdn_244 (Progenitus, MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent replacement), fdn_61 (HighSocietyHunter, AttacksTriggeredEvent), fdn_141 (Giada, get_mana_abilities with `_cost(game, src)`/`_mana_produced(game)`), fdn_91 (Kellan, get_activated_abilities animate via subtypes/modified_power mutation), fdn_6 (ClawsOut, end-of-turn ContinuousEffect +2/+2 via effect_manager.add).\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **sos_1 negative cost-reduction test failed**: expected `CastingError` but `test_utils.cast_spell` wraps the underlying CastingError in `TestSetupError` (\"Failed to cast 'The Dawning Archaic': ... insufficient mana\"). Fixed by importing `TestSetupError as _TestSetupError` and catching `(CastingError, _TestSetupError)`.\n   - **pytest collection warning**: importing `TestSetupError` directly caused \"cannot collect test class 'TestSetupError'\". Fixed by aliasing to `_TestSetupError`.\n   - **Design risk avoided (sos_257)**: A naive `power`/`toughness` property returning 0 when not animate