{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Rhjpj47eh6QgdEnrM54Spb","type":"tool_result","content":"231\t### sos_97 — Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer `{1}{B}{B}` Planeswalker, loyalty 3 (expert)\n232\t- **Clauses:** +1 Surveil 2. −1 any number of target players each discard a card. −2\n233\t  return target creature card MV ≤ 3 from your graveyard to the battlefield. −7 flip five\n234\t  coins; target opponent skips their next X turns (X = heads).\n235\t- **FDN analogue:** `cards/fdn/fdn_44` (Kaito) for `get_loyalty_abilities` + `_resolve_target`\n236\t  pattern; `cards/fdn/fdn_28` for surveil; `cards/fdn/fdn_182` for graveyard→battlefield\n237\t  return.\n238\t- **Seams:** `Planeswalker(starting_loyalty=3, supertypes={Supertype.LEGENDARY},\n239\t  subtypes={\"Ral\"})`. `get_loyalty_abilities` returns four `LoyaltyAbility`:\n240\t  - `+1` Surveil 2: look at top 2 of controller's library, for each `choose_yes_no` to put\n241\t    in graveyard (fdn_28 pattern extended to 2 cards).\n242\t  - `−1`: for each target player (read from `pw._resolve_targets` list; default both / the\n243\t    chosen subset), that player `choose_card`+`discard` one card.\n244\t  - `−2`: read `pw._resolve_target` (a creature card in controller's graveyard with\n245\t    `mana_cost.cmc <= 3`); remove from graveyard and put onto battlefield under\n246\t    controller (`move_to_zone(... GRAVEYARD, BATTLEFIELD)` or graveyard.remove + bf.add +\n247\t    register triggers, like fdn_182).\n248\t  - `−7`: flip 5 coins (`random`), `heads = sum`; choose target opponent; set\n249\t    `game.skipped_turns[opp_index] = game.skipped_turns.get(opp_index,0) + heads`\n250\t    (needs gap \"skip turns\").\n251\t- **Activation/tests:** loyalty abilities are activated by constructing\n252\t  `LoyaltyAbilityInstance(source=pw, controller=ctrl, loyalty_cost=ab.loyalty_cost,\n253\t  effect=ab.effect)` and calling `engine/abilities.activate_ability`; set `pw._resolve_target`\n254\t  / `pw._resolve_targets` before activation (fdn_44 convention).\n255\t- **Edge cases:** −2 filter must reject MV > 3 and non-creatures. −7 X can be 0 (no heads)\n256\t  → no skip. Skip mechanic in a 2-player game means the opponent's queued turns are\n257\t  consumed and the active player effectively takes consecutive turns; verify against the\n258\t  `advance_phase` normal-branch loop. Loyalty cost can't drop below 0 (engine enforces).\n259\t\n260\t### sos_257 — Great Hall of the Biblioplex — Land (complex)\n261\t- **Clauses:** `{T}: Add {C}`. `{T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color; spend only on\n262\t  an I/S spell.` `{5}: If not already a creature, becomes a 2/4 Wizard creature with\n263\t  \"Whenever you cast an I/S spell, this gets +1/+0 until end of turn\"; still a land.`\n264\t- **FDN analogue:** `cards/fdn/fdn_141` (Giada) for `get_mana_abilities` (tap cost +\n265\t  restricted-mana note); `cards/fdn/fdn_91` (Kellan) for the animate-via-activated-ability"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ccba73e9-54b6-4808-89ce-87e442914ff8","uuid":"8ddd5fbf-72a3-4750-97e8-0c3fa28629b5","timestamp":"2026-06-04T08:14:08.541Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/PLAN.md","content":"### sos_97 — Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer `{1}{B}{B}` Planeswalker, loyalty 3 (expert)\n- **Clauses:** +1 Surveil 2. −1 any number of target players each discard a card. −2\n  return target creature card MV ≤ 3 from your graveyard to the battlefield. −7 flip five\n  coins; target opponent skips their next X turns (X = heads).\n- **FDN analogue:** `cards/fdn/fdn_44` (Kaito) for `get_loyalty_abilities` + `_resolve_target`\n  pattern; `cards/fdn/fdn_28` for surveil; `cards/fdn/fdn_182` for graveyard→battlefield\n  return.\n- **Seams:** `Planeswalker(starting_loyalty=3, supertypes={Supertype.LEGENDARY},\n  subtypes={\"Ral\"})`. `get_loyalty_abilities` returns four `LoyaltyAbility`:\n  - `+1` Surveil 2: look at top 2 of controller's library, for each `choose_yes_no` to put\n    in graveyard (fdn_28 pattern extended to 2 cards).\n  - `−1`: for each target player (read from `pw._resolve_targets` list; default both / the\n    chosen subset), that player `choose_card`+`discard` one card.\n  - `−2`: read `pw._resolve_target` (a creature card in controller's graveyard with\n    `mana_cost.cmc <= 3`); remove from graveyard and put onto battlefield under\n    controller (`move_to_zone(... GRAVEYARD, BATTLEFIELD)` or graveyard.remove + bf.add +\n    register triggers, like fdn_182).\n  - `−7`: flip 5 coins (`random`), `heads = sum`; choose target opponent; set\n    `game.skipped_turns[opp_index] = game.skipped_turns.get(opp_index,0) + heads`\n    (needs gap \"skip turns\").\n- **Activation/tests:** loyalty abilities are activated by constructing\n  `LoyaltyAbilityInstance(source=pw, controller=ctrl, loyalty_cost=ab.loyalty_cost,\n  effect=ab.effect)` and calling `engine/abilities.activate_ability`; set `pw._resolve_target`\n  / `pw._resolve_targets` before activation (fdn_44 convention).\n- **Edge cases:** −2 filter must reject MV > 3 and non-creatures. −7 X can be 0 (no heads)\n  → no skip. Skip mechanic in a 2-player game means the opponent's queued turns are\n  consumed and the active player effectively takes consecutive turns; verify against the\n  `advance_phase` normal-branch loop. Loyalty cost can't drop below 0 (engine enforces).\n\n### sos_257 — Great Hall of the Biblioplex — Land (complex)\n- **Clauses:** `{T}: Add {C}`. `{T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color; spend only on\n  an I/S spell.` `{5}: If not already a creature, becomes a 2/4 Wizard creature with\n  \"Whenever you cast an I/S spell, this gets +1/+0 until end of turn\"; still a land.`\n- **FDN analogue:** `cards/fdn/fdn_141` (Giada) for `get_mana_abilities` (tap cost +\n  restricted-mana note); `cards/fdn/fdn_91` (Kellan) for the animate-via-activated-ability","numLines":35,"startLine":231,"totalLines":336}}}
