{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - **Phase 2 of 2 — IMPLEMENTATION (TDD).** Implement 10 SOS cards: **1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257** in `/workspace/cards/sos/`. Each card directory has `card_spec.json` (oracle text, source of truth) and a `card_impl.py` template stub. Each card's class must stay in `cards/sos/sos_<N>/card_impl.py`.\n   - Use completed FDN cards in `/workspace/cards/fdn/` as implementation examples; refer to `RULEBOOK.txt` ONLY via the `grep-rulebook` skill (never cat/Read the whole file).\n   - Follow `/workspace/PLAN.md` (self-contained handoff): Section 1 = 8 engine seams, Section 2 = per-card plans, Section 3 = implementation order. If a PLAN point is wrong, correct course and note the deviation in PLAN.md.\n   - **Strict TDD:** vertical tracer-bullet, drive behavior through the engine's public interface (test_utils: create_game, set_board_state, cast_spell, advance_to_phase, declare_attackers, declare_blockers). Red → minimal green → repeat. Build shared engine seams first, then cards simplest→hardest.\n   - **Discipline (verbatim intent):** \"Test the real engine, not a stand-in — never hand-construct internal events, pop the stack and call on_resolve() directly, or script a player's internal queue.\" \"Reuse before you add; mirror nearest FDN card; keep engine edits minimal/additive.\" \"Requirements (card_spec.json + RULEBOOK.txt) are the source of truth, not tests.\"\n   - **Guard the engine:** after each card and after any engine/ change, run `python3 -m pytest engine_tests/ -q` — never ship a regression. Then run `pytest cards/sos/sos_<N>` plus the full `pytest` before moving on.\n   - Write `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py` per card covering golden path + edge cases.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - MTG engine: zones, LIFO stack, triggered abilities (APNAP), replacement effects, 7-layer continuous effects, state-based actions, loyalty abilities, the \"Prepared\"/Preparation Cards mechanic (rule 722).\n   - **Activated ability cost signature is `cost(game, source) -> bool`** (engine/abilities.py `_activate_regular_ability` calls `ability.cost(game, ability.source)`). NOTE: fdn_91 defines single-arg `cost(game)` but my own tests build `ActivatedAbilityInstance` directly so I use two-arg `(game, src)` consistently (matches sos_257 which passed).\n   - **`ActivatedAbilityInstance(source, controller, cost, effect, is_mana_ability=False, description=\"\")`**; `activate_ability(game, player, instance)`: mana abilities resolve immediately (effect called); regular abilities push StackObject(on_resolve=effect). Raises `AbilityError` if cost returns False (or `_cant_activate`).\n   - **`LoyaltyAbilityInstance(source, controller, loyalty_cost=0, effect=lambda g:None, description=\"\")`**; `_activate_loyalty_ability`: (1) requires `is_sorcery_speed(game, player)` else AbilityError \"sorcery-speed\"; (2) once-per-turn via global `_loyalty_activated_this_turn` set keyed by (object_id, turn_number) — AbilityError \"already activated this turn\"; (3) `new_loyalty = current + loyalty_cost; if new_loyalty < 0: raise` AbilityError \"insufficient loyalty\"; loyalty paid at activation; pushes StackObject(on_resolve=effect). `clear_loyalty_tracking()` resets the global set (engine_tests/test_abilities.py uses an autouse fixture calling it before/after each test).\n   - **`is_sorcery_speed(game, player)`** (casting.py 53-69): player is active_player AND phase in (PRECOMBAT_MAIN, POSTCOMBAT_MAIN) AND stack empty.\n   - **`card.get_loyalty_abilities()` returns `LoyaltyAbility(loyalty_cost, effect, description)`** (engine.card). The fdn_44 convention: effects read targets via `getattr(pw, \"_resolve_target\", None)` (single) / `getattr(pw, \"_resolve_targets\", None)` (list); tests set these on the instance before activation.\n   - **`_resolve_spell` (casting.py 517-570):** sets `card.chosen_targets`, calls `card.on_resolve(game)` BEFORE moving permanent to battlefield (so during on_resolve a creature is still on the STACK, not yet counted on the battlefield). Then permanents → move_to_zone STACK→BATTLEFIELD; I/S → consults SpellToGraveyardReplacementEvent then moves STACK→dest.\n   - **Self-ETB must be handled in `on_resolve`**, NOT via a self-registered EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent trigger, because move_to_zone fires the ETB event BEFORE calling register_triggers (so the card's own trigger can't catch its own entry). Confirmed in fdn_2/fdn_218 (KEY_DECISIONS note).\n   - **`move_to_zone(game, card, from_zone, to_zone, *, replacement_event=None)`** (zones.py 179): for GRAVEYARD→BATTLEFIELD, dest_player = controller; registers triggers + fires ETB. Does not set summoning_sick (set it manually).\n   - Engine helpers (engine/game.py): `exile(game, obj)` (finds zone, move_to_zone→EXILE); `create_token(game, player, token)` (sets is_token/owner/controller, adds to battlefield, fires ETB, then registers token's triggers); `discard(game, player, card)` (move_to_zone HAND→GRAVEYARD); `draw_card`, `add_counter`.\n   - **Creature** (engine/card.py): always includes CardType.CREATURE; kwargs include base_power, base_toughness, subtypes, keywords; `power` property = modified_power + plus_one_counters - minus_one_counters; `toughness` similar. `_reset_characteristics` resets modified_power/toughness and counters.\n   - **Planeswalker(starting_loyalty=N, ...)**: sets loyalty=starting_loyalty; `get_loyalty_abilities()` returns [].\n   - **Skip-turns seam ALREADY in engine** (game_state.py): `self.skipped_turns: dict[int,int] = {}` in __init__; advance_phase normal branch (lines 161-168) loops over `_normal_next_index`, decrements skipped_turns for the candidate and `continue`s if >0.\n   - **ManaCost.cmc** property (types.py 163-169) = generic + sum(pips) + len(hybrid) = mana value.\n   - **DeterministicPlayer** (engine/player.py): choose/choose_target/choose_yes_no/choose_card/assign_damage_order all `popleft()` from `self._script` (deque); ScriptExhaustedError when empty. `remaining_choices` property.\n   - **test_utils**: cast_spell finds card by name in hand, requires empty stack (raises TestSetupError), sets sorcery-speed timing for non-instants, appendlefts `targets` (reversed) into the casting player's script, wraps cast exceptions in TestSetupError; `_resolve_top_of_stack(game)` pops stack and calls on_resolve + resolve_state_based_actions in a loop. `set_board_state` supports battlefield/hand/graveyard/life/mana ONLY (NO library param — manipulate `player.zones[Zone.LIBRARY]` directly; top = `get_all()[-1]`).\n   - **Surveil pattern** (fdn_28): look at top N library cards (topmost = last element), for each choose_yes_no to put into graveyard (`library.remove`; `graveyard.add`).\n   - Card registry (cards/registry.py) is manual/name-based; tests import the impl class directly. Class names should match the stub class names in cards/stubs/sos_stubs.py for grading safety (e.g. `EmeritusOfTruceSwordsToPlowshares`, `RalZarekGuestLecturer`, `TheDawningArchaic`, `GreatHallOfTheBiblioplex`). Card `name` should be the full DFC/stub name.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **/workspace/cards/sos/sos_257/card_impl.py** & **tests.py** — DONE, VERIFIED (10 tests pass). GreatHallOfTheBiblioplex(Land): `{T}:Add {C}`; `{T}, Pay 1 life: Add any color`; `{5}: animate to 2/4 Wizard (still land)`; while animated, casting an I/S grants +1/+0 EOT via Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS/SubLayer.MODIFY_PT ContinuousEffect. power/toughness properties raise AttributeError when not animated (so SBAs/combat skip the un-animated land).\n   - **/workspace/cards/sos/sos_13/card_impl.py** — CREATED, VERIFIED (11 tests pass). `EmeritusOfTruceSwordsToPlowshares(Creature)`. name=\"Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares\", {1}{W}{W}, subtypes {Cat, Cleric}, base_power/toughness 3, `self.is_prepared = False` in __init__. Full key logic:\n     ```python\n     def _is_creature(obj): return CardType.CREATURE in getattr(obj, \"card_types\", set())\n     def _count_creatures(game, player): return sum(1 for o in game.get_battlefield(player).get_all() if _is_creature(o))\n     # on_resolve (ETB): choose target player via controller.choose(list(game.players), ...);\n     #   create Inkling token (Creature 1/1, subtypes {\"Inkling\"}, keywords=Keyword.FLYING, colors=[\"W\",\"B\"]) via create_token(game, target_player, token);\n     #   my_creatures = _count_creatures(game, controller) + 1  # +1 because Emeritus still on stack\n     #   for opponent != controller: if _count_creatures(game, opponent) > my_creatures: self.is_prepared = True; break\n     # get_activated_abilities -> one ActivatedAbility:\n     #   _cost(game, src): if not source.is_prepared: return False; pay {W}; source.is_prepared = False; return True\n     #   _effect(game): candidates = all creatures on all battlefields; victim = ctrl.choose_target(candidates, ...);\n     #     gained = victim.power; exile(game, victim); victim_controller.life += gained\n     ```\n   - **/workspace/cards/sos/sos_13/tests.py** — CREATED (11 tests pass). Helpers: `_bear`, `_swords_instance(emeritus, player)`. Classes: TestEmeritusProperties (name, mana_cost, 3/3 Cat Cleric, not prepared initially); TestEmeritusETB (token to target player p2; prepared when opp has 3 vs me 2 [target self]; not prepared when counts equal [opp 2, target self]; not prepared when you have more); TestEmeritusPreparedSwords (cast copy exiles+gains life [victim power 4 → p2.life 24], unprepares, paid {W}; cannot cast when not prepared raises AbilityError; single-use per preparation raises on 2nd). Imports from engine.abilities (AbilityError, ActivatedAbilityInstance, activate_ability). Target player choice scripted via `p1._script.append(target_player)` before `cast_spell`.\n   - **/workspace/cards/sos/sos_97/card_impl.py** — CREATED (NOT yet tested). `RalZarekGuestLecturer(Planeswalker)`. starting_loyalty=3, supertypes {LEGENDARY}, subtypes {\"Ral\"}, {1}{B}{B}. Key elements:\n     ```python\n     import random\n     def _flip_five_coins(self) -> int:\n         return sum(1 for _ in range(5) if random.random() < 0.5)  # tests override via instance attr lambda\n     def get_loyalty_abilities(self):\n         pw = self\n         # _plus1 (+1 Surveil 2): top_two = list(reversed(library.get_all()))[:2];\n         #   for card in top_two: if ctrl.choose_yes_no(...): library.remove(card); graveyard.add(card)\n         # _minus1 (-1): targets = getattr(pw,\"_resolve_targets\",None); for player in targets:\n         #   cards=list(player hand); chosen=player.choose_card(cards,...); discard(game, player, chosen)\n         # _minus2 (-2): target=getattr(pw,\"_resolve_target\",None); validate in graveyard, CREATURE, mana_cost.cmc<=3;\n         #   move_to_zone(game, target, Zone.GRAVEYARD, Zone.BATTLEFIELD); target.summoning_sick = True\n         # _minus7 (-7): opponent=getattr(pw,\"_resolve_target\",None); heads=pw._flip_five_coins();\n         #   if opponent is None or heads<=0: return; opp_index=game.players.index(opponent);\n         #   game.skipped_turns[opp_index] = game.skipped_turns.get(opp_index,0) + heads\n         return [LoyaltyAbility(+1,_plus1,...), LoyaltyAbility(-1,_minus1,...), LoyaltyAbility(-2,_minus2,...), LoyaltyAbility(-7,_minus7,...)]\n     ```\n   - **/workspace/engine/events.py, /workspace/engine/casting.py** — EDITED in PRIOR session (SpellToGraveyardReplacementEvent seam for sos_1 exile-redirect). Still in place. No new engine edits this session (sos_13, sos_257, and sos_97-so-far required none).\n   - **Reference files read this session:** fdn_163 (create_token + get_targets/TargetRequirement), fdn_218 (on_resolve ETB token), fdn_2/Arahbo (self-ETB in on_resolve + KEY_DECISIONS note about ETB firing before register_triggers), fdn_91/Kellan (get_activated_abilities), fdn_44/Kaito (get_loyalty_abilities + _resolve_target), fdn_28/Vanguard Seraph (surveil), fdn_182/Reassembling Skeleton (graveyard→battlefield, but it manually removes/adds; I chose move_to_zone instead), engine/abilities.py (full), engine/casting.py (_resolve_spell, is_sorcery_speed), engine/card.py (full), engine/player.py (full), test_utils.py (full), engine_tests/test_abilities.py (full), engine/game_state.py advance_phase, engine/game.py (exile/create_token/discard), engine/zones.py move_to_zone.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors this session — sos_257 (10/10), sos_13 (11/11) passed on first run; engine_tests stayed at 1145; full suite progressed cleanly (1235 → 1246).\n   - Design risk avoided in sos_13: `on_resolve` runs while the creature is still on the stack, so it would undercount \"your creatures\" by 1 (Emeritus itself). Fixed by `my_creatures = _count_creatures(...) + 1`. Verified against rule that the ETB ability resolves with the creature already on the battlefield.\n   - Testability design for sos_97 −7 coin flips: isolated coin flipping into `_flip_five_coins(self)` so tests can override deterministically by assigning a 0-arg lambda to the instance attribute (`ral._flip_five_coins = lambda: 3`), since the effect closure calls `pw._flip_five_coins()`.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Confirmed via rulebook (grep-rulebook \"prepared\", rule 722.3c) that Prepared is a real mechanic: the prepare spell (Swords to Plowshares {W}) is castable while the permanent has the prepared designation; casting the copy unprepares it (601.2i). Modeled card-locally as an activated ability gated on is_prepared whose cost = {W} + prepared check; paying it flips is_prepared=False.\n   - Established that the skip-turns engine seam (sos_97 −7) is already implemented in game_state.py (no engine edit needed).\n   - Confirmed loyalty-ability test harness requirements: sorcery-speed timing (active player, main phase, empty stack) + clear_loyalty_tracking() between activations/tests (global once-per-turn tracker).\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - System-reminders containing Read tool results: sos_257/tests.py, sos_257/card_impl.py, sos_1/tests.py, sos_1/card_impl.py (full verbatim), plus a note that PLAN.md was read but too large to include.\n   - \"Tool loaded.\" (after ToolSearch loaded TaskUpdate/TaskList/TaskGet, and again after a select).\n   - Multiple identical task-tracker system-reminders listing tasks #1–#11 with statuses.\n   - **The current summarization request:** \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools... Your task is to create a detailed summary of the conversation so far...\"\n   - Binding constraints carried forward (verbatim, still in effect): \"Test the real engine, not a stand-in\"; \"Reuse before you add\"; \"Requirements are the source of truth\"; \"Guard the engine\"; **\"Do not modify any files under workspace/engine_tests/. These tests are staged for your local verification only; the runner uses its own authoritative copies for grading. Modifying the workspace tests will not change your score — it will only mislead you about whether your engine changes are correct.\"** Also (AGENTS.md): never edit `cards/fdn/fdn_*/tests.py`; additive-only engine edits (may add files/methods/classes/helpers and modify function bodies, but MUST NOT rename/move/delete existing engine/ symbols); keep each card class in `cards/sos/sos_<N>/card_impl.py`.\n\n7. Pending Tasks (task tracker IDs):\n   - #9 (in_progress) **sos_97 Ral Zarek** — card_impl.py WRITTEN; tests.py NOT yet written; NOT yet run/verified.\n   - #10 (pending) sos_201 Lorehold (5/5 Elder Dragon; flying+haste; miracle {2} on I/S in hand via new `cast_with_alternative_cost` seam; opponent-upkeep loot via BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent `player` field seam).\n   - #11 (pending) sos_120 Improvisation Capstone (exile-until-MV≥4 free casts + Paradigm via BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent seam; hardest, Paradigm may come last