{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01761dWkwnJPCRFG9qBn4Cd7","type":"tool_result","content":"205\t  exiled original; create a token-copy or re-castable copy). \"First resolve\" → register the\n206\t  Paradigm trigger only once. This is the hardest part; Paradigm may be implemented after\n207\t  the base spell works.\n208\t\n209\t### sos_201 — Lorehold, the Historian `{3}{R}{W}` 5/5 Elder Dragon (expert)\n210\t- **Clauses:** Flying, haste. \"Each instant and sorcery card in your hand has miracle {2}.\"\n211\t  \"At the beginning of each opponent's upkeep, you may discard a card; if you do, draw a\n212\t  card.\"\n213\t- **FDN analogue:** opponent-upkeep loot — `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent`/upkeep trigger\n214\t  patterns (fdn_28 surveil shows draw-trigger + choose plumbing); miracle uses the new\n215\t  `cast_with_alternative_cost`.\n216\t- **Seams:** `keywords=Keyword.FLYING|Keyword.HASTE`. `register_triggers`: (a)\n217\t  `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent` trigger (needs gap \"upkeep player field\"); condition\n218\t  `event.player is not self.controller`; effect: `choose_yes_no` → if yes pick a card to\n219\t  discard (`choose_card`), `discard`, then `draw_card`. (b) Miracle: register a\n220\t  `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent` trigger; condition: `event.player is self.controller`, the\n221\t  drawn `event.card` is I/S and owned by controller, and it is the first card drawn this\n222\t  turn (`event.player.cards_drawn_this_turn == 1` — engine increments before firing).\n223\t  Effect: `choose_yes_no(\"Cast for miracle {2}?\")`; if yes,\n224\t  `cast_with_alternative_cost(game, controller, event.card, ManaCost(generic=2))`.\n225\t- **Edge cases:** miracle only applies while Lorehold is on the battlefield and the card is\n226\t  in *your* hand at draw time. Only the first draw of the turn qualifies. Opponent-upkeep\n227\t  loot is \"may\" and only draws if you discarded. Haste lets the dragon attack the turn it\n228\t  enters (engine already