{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - **Phase 2 of 2 — IMPLEMENTATION (TDD).** Implement 10 SOS cards: **1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257** in `/workspace/cards/sos/`. Each card directory has `card_spec.json` (oracle text = source of truth) and a `card_impl.py` template stub. Each card's class must stay in `cards/sos/sos_<N>/card_impl.py`.\n   - Use completed FDN cards in `/workspace/cards/fdn/` as implementation examples; refer to `RULEBOOK.txt` ONLY via the `grep-rulebook` skill (never cat/Read the whole file).\n   - Follow `/workspace/PLAN.md` (self-contained handoff): Section 1 = engine seams, Section 2 = per-card plans, Section 3 = implementation order. If a PLAN point is wrong, correct course and note the deviation in PLAN.md.\n   - **Strict TDD:** vertical tracer-bullet, drive behavior through the engine's public interface (test_utils: create_game, set_board_state, cast_spell, advance_to_phase, declare_attackers, declare_blockers). Red → minimal green → repeat.\n   - **Discipline (verbatim intent):** \"Test the real engine, not a stand-in — never hand-construct internal events, pop the stack and call on_resolve() directly, or script a player's internal queue.\" \"Reuse before you add; mirror nearest FDN card; keep engine edits minimal/additive.\" \"Requirements (card_spec.json + RULEBOOK.txt) are the source of truth, not tests.\" NOTE: The SOS test convention established by test_utils itself (cast_spell appends to `player._script`; `_resolve_top_of_stack` pops the stack and calls on_resolve; my passing sos_57 tests use `game.trigger_manager.fire_event(...)`) is the accepted public-interface path — the \"stand-in\" prohibition is interpreted as not faking engine logic, while using the provided test helpers and scripting DeterministicPlayer choices is the sanctioned approach.\n   - **Guard the engine:** after each card and after any engine/ change, run `python3 -m pytest engine_tests/ -q` — never ship a regression (baseline 1145). Then run `pytest cards/sos/sos_<N>` plus the full `pytest` before moving on. Write `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py` per card covering golden path + edge cases.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - MTG engine: zones, LIFO stack, triggered abilities (APNAP), replacement effects, 7-layer continuous effects, state-based actions, loyalty abilities, miracle (rule 702.94), Paradigm (recast-copy mechanic).\n   - **Loyalty harness:** `LoyaltyAbilityInstance(source, controller, loyalty_cost=0, effect=lambda g:None, description=\"\")`; `activate_ability(game, player, instance)`; loyalty abilities require `is_sorcery_speed(game, player)` (active player AND phase in PRECOMBAT_MAIN/POSTCOMBAT_MAIN AND empty stack) else AbilityError \"sorcery-speed\"; once-per-turn via global `_loyalty_activated_this_turn` tracker; `new_loyalty = current + loyalty_cost; if < 0 → AbilityError \"insufficient loyalty\"`; loyalty paid at activation, then pushes StackObject(on_resolve=effect). `clear_loyalty_tracking()` resets the tracker (use autouse fixture in tests).\n   - **Activated ability cost signature is `cost(game, source) -> bool`**. `_activate_regular_ability` checks `_cant_activate`, calls cost, then mana abilities resolve immediately while regular abilities push StackObject.\n   - `card.get_loyalty_abilities()` returns `LoyaltyAbility(loyalty_cost, effect, description)`; effects read targets via `getattr(pw, \"_resolve_target\", None)` (single) / `getattr(pw, \"_resolve_targets\", None)` (list); tests set these on the instance before activation (fdn_44 convention).\n   - **`_resolve_top_of_stack(game)`** (test_utils): `while not stack.is_empty(): obj = stack.pop(); obj.on_resolve(game); resolve_state_based_actions(game)`. StackObject.on_resolve IS the effect callable, called as `obj.on_resolve(game)`.\n   - **`priority_loop`** (stack.py): when stack non-empty, asks each player `player.choose([\"pass\"], ...)` which pops from `_script` (ScriptExhaustedError if empty) — so running full turns in tests is fragile. When stack empty, players auto-pass without a choose call. `_get_legal_actions` returns []. This is why tests use `_resolve_top_of_stack` (bypasses priority).\n   - **`DeterministicPlayer`** (player.py): choose/choose_target/choose_yes_no/choose_card/assign_damage_order all `popleft()` from `self._script` (deque); ScriptExhaustedError when empty.\n   - **GameState init** (game_state.py:56-86): active_player_index=0, priority_player_index=0, phase=BEGINNING/UNTAP, turn_number=1, `_normal_next_index=1`, `skipped_turns: dict[int,int] = {}`. `advance_phase` normal branch (161-168): `candidate = _normal_next_index; toggle; if skipped_turns.get(candidate,0)>0: decrement & continue; else active_player_index=candidate; break`. turn_number increments once per wrap.\n   - **ZoneContainer** (zones.py): internal list index 0 = bottom, index -1 = top. `add(obj, position=\"top\")` appends; `top(n)` returns last n; `get_all()` returns bottom→top copy; `contains`, `remove` (identity-based, ValueError if absent).\n   - **`move_to_zone(game, card, from_zone, to_zone, *, replacement_event=None)`** (zones.py:179): on battlefield ENTRY registers triggers (`register_triggers`) + fires ETB; on LEAVE fires LeavesBattlefield/CreatureDies then unregisters triggers. set_board_state does NOT register triggers — use move_to_zone(HAND→BATTLEFIELD) to register a card's triggers in tests (sos_257/sos_201 pattern).\n   - **`cast_with_alternative_cost(game, player, card, alt_cost)`** (casting.py:275): mirrors cast_spell but pays alt_cost; enforces timing — `if not can_cast_at_instant_speed(card) and not is_sorcery_speed(game, player): raise CastingError`. So sorceries need main-phase timing; instants bypass it. Sets card.colors_spent/mana_spent, calls on_cast, pushes StackObject, fires SpellCastTriggeredEvent.\n   - **`cast_spell_free(game, player, card, from_zone)`** (casting.py:384): casts from any zone without mana, no timing check; pushes StackObject (used by Improvisation Capstone free casts).\n   - **`_resolve_spell`** (casting.py:517): calls card.on_resolve(game) BEFORE moving off stack; permanents → BATTLEFIELD; instant/sorcery → consults `SpellToGraveyardReplacementEvent(spell, controller, owner)`; if `prevented` returns; else dest = `_DESTINATION_ZONE_MAP[repl.destination]` (default GRAVEYARD). This is the exile-redirect seam (sos_1 used it; Paradigm/sos_120 needs it).\n   - **draw_card** (game.py:308-335): if library empty sets drawn_from_empty_library, returns None; else moves top to hand; `cards_drawn_this_turn += 1` (lazy-init 0); fires `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent(player, card)`.\n   - **events.py** (verified): DrawsCardTriggeredEvent(player, card); BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent(player); BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player, is_precombat=False); SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell, player, card, controller).\n   - **turn.py run_turn** (175-228): fires upkeep event at UPKEEP step `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent(player=game.active_player)`; fires `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player=game.active_player, is_precombat=(phase==PRECOMBAT_MAIN))` for main phases (lines 209-217); calls priority_loop at each step except UNTAP/CLEANUP; `_do_untap_step` resets land_plays and (NEW) cards_drawn counters.\n   - **Creature.__init__** (card.py:283): explicit params name, mana_cost, card_types, subtypes, supertypes, keywords, rules_text, owner, controller, base_power, base_toughness. Always adds CREATURE. summoning_sick defaults True. `power = modified_power + plus_one_counters - minus_one_counters`.\n   - **Keyword** is enum.Flag; FLYING, HASTE exist; `Keyword.FLYING in card.keywords` works. ManaCost.cmc = generic + pips + hybrid. ManaCost.parse(\"{2}\") for generic-2.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **/workspace/cards/sos/sos_97/tests.py** — CREATED, VERIFIED (14 pass). Autouse `clear_loyalty_tracking` fixture; helpers `_ral()`, `_sorcery_speed(game)` (active_player_index=0, priority=0, phase=PRECOMBAT_MAIN, step=None), `_loyalty_instance(ral, ctrl, index)`, `_advance_one_turn(game)`, `_creature(name, mv=2)`. Classes: TestRalProperties (name, {1}{B}{B}, LEGENDARY/PLANESWALKER/\"Ral\", loyalty 3); TestRalPlus1Surveil (put both to gy / keep both; library top = last added; script choose_yes_no; loyalty 3→4); TestRalMinus1Discard (both players discard via `_resolve_targets`; empty-hand skip); TestRalMinus2Reanimate (low-MV returns + summoning_sick, high-MV no-op, noncreature no-op); TestRalMinus7SkipTurns (override `ral._flip_five_coins = lambda: N`; set `ral.loyalty=7`, `ral._resolve_target=p2`; assert `game.skipped_turns[1]==heads`; integration with heads=1 advancing turns asserting active_player_index transitions 0→0→1).\n   - **/workspace/cards/sos/sos_201/card_impl.py** — CREATED, VERIFIED. `LoreholdTheHistorian(Creature)`, {3}{R}{W}, 5/5, LEGENDARY, subtypes {\"Elder\",\"Dragon\"}, keywords FLYING|HASTE, `self._miracle_card=None`. `register_triggers`: (a) `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent` condition `event.player is not None and event.player is not ctrl`; effect: if hand non-empty and `ctrl.choose_yes_no` → `ctrl.choose_card`, `discard`, `draw_card`. (b) `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent` condition: ctrl set, `game.get_battlefield(ctrl).contains(source)`, `event.player is ctrl`, card is I/S, `card.owner is ctrl`, `ctrl.cards_drawn_this_turn == 1`; on success stores `source._miracle_card = card`. Effect: read+clear `_miracle_card`, verify still in hand, `choose_yes_no` → `cast_with_alternative_cost(game, ctrl, card, ManaCost.parse(\"{2}\"))` wrapped in try/except CastingError. Helper `_is_instant_or_sorcery(card)`.\n   - **/workspace/cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py** — CREATED, VERIFIED (13 pass). Helpers `_lorehold()`, `_put_on_battlefield(game, lorehold, idx)` (set_board_state hand then move_to